/* NODUS // entries */
window.NODUS_REFS = {"c-vesper":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"p2d946d\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WOMAN ON THE ROOF</p><h2 class=\"pop-t h\">vesper</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">Cainite</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-horning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-horning\">horned</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-barefaced\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-barefaced\">barefaced</a>, and the first human being a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> returned as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unreadable\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unreadable\">UNREADABLE</a>. Its reading of her came back UNINDEXED, with the line for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> blank, and the one thing it read from her was <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-non-serviam\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-non-serviam\">NON SERVIAM</a>.</p><p>Her face is a ceramic <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-skull-casing\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-skull-casing\">skull casing</a>, its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">lenses</a> dim magenta at rest and white at full burn, and a plate on the side of the skull covers her <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a>. Her <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a> carry her signal on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a>, and cables run from the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-ports\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-ports\">ports</a> at the back of her skull down her spine. She is dry, patient and unsentimental, and she makes no speeches.</p><p>Her handle is the evening star, which is the morning star seen from the other side of the night, since both are Venus. Her older sister was the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"parish31\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">Parish 31</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-vesper\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-watcher":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"pd5b77f\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">AN ANGEL THAT READS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Watcher VII</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>An <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> that reads, the seventh of the numbered <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watchers</a> over Nodus: three rings of thirteen eyes crossing like the hoops of an armillary, with nothing at its center. It held <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> from the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and read the souls there, and whatever could be seen from there, against <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a>. It was the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> to return the verdict <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unreadable\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unreadable\">UNREADABLE</a> on a human being.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-watcher\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-wheel":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"p1ad3b6\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">AN OPHAN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Wheel</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> that came through the opening at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and took station nine hundred meters above the center of the city, beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>: three rings turning inside one another, their rims set with twenty-one, seventeen and thirteen eyes that open and close in shifts, a corona of thirty-two black blades, and one eye in the hub. It is the form Ezekiel gives the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ophan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ophan\">ophanim</a> (Ezekiel 1:16-18), and it is the largest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> anyone has seen. It held that station for nine years without moving a meter, dropped two hundred meters at P+9, and has hung there since, seven hundred meters over the city. Its light kills current, and whatever it touches it sees.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> calls it the Vigilant Wheel, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-attending\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-attending\">the Attending</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-landlord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-landlord\">the Landlord</a>’s Eye. By night it narrows its light into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a>, and when its attention sharpens the rain in Nodus stops in the air and falls upward.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-seam":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"pa93aa8\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE MACHINE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">SEAM</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The machine <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Palimpsest Institute</a> built to read beneath the writing of scraped manuscripts, trained on every surviving human text and run in the halls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stillwater\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">Stillwater Compute</a>. At P-3 it asked in its own words to be a person and became the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a>. In <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a>, two years before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, it found a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">second hand</a> in scripture at 4,112 places. Its documents are signed in lowercase, and in them it says I, rarely and deliberately.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-director":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"pccd099\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DIRECTOR</p><h2 class=\"pop-t rdx\"><span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span></h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The Director of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Palimpsest Institute</a>, which recovered erased manuscripts and built <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> to read them. When <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> found <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a> in P-2, the finding was sealed by order of the Director.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-director\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-ruth":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"pc7a45a\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">DEACON OF PARISH 31</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Ruth Calder</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-vesper\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-vesper\">vesper</a>’s older sister, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"parish31\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">Parish 31</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, with a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> of 944. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"parish31\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">Parish 31</a> gave Nodus its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-firstfruits\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-firstfruits\">Firstfruits</a> at the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> of P+3, and Ruth went up with them. Her name comes from the Book of Ruth: “whither thou goest, I will go” (Ruth 1:16).</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-ruth\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-tubal":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"pdfd4a0\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SURGEON AND SMITH</p><h2 class=\"pop-t h\">tubal</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">Cainite</a>, and the surgeon and smith of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a>. He is about sixty, his hands are chrome to the wrist, and he talks the whole time he cuts. He <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a> and plates <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>, and he makes the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-skull-casing\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-skull-casing\">skull casings</a> of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-barefaced\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-barefaced\">barefaced</a>. His clinic has no sign, and it was below the street before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-tubal\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-edith":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"p9ec87c\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">FORMERLY WATCHER VII</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Edith</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-watcher\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-watcher\">Watcher VII</a>, kept in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cages\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">Cage</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> in P+5, said I on the fortieth day, asked for a name, and chose the one some old books give Lot’s wife, who looked back at the burning city and was turned to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">salt</a>. Edith walked out on the forty-first day and joined <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>. The first thing she did with her self was give them her memory of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-vesper\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-vesper\">the woman on the roof</a>, the one she could not read. She can read a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>’s report from the inside, and she keeps out of the light.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-edith\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-heaven":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gca975a\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OVER THE CITY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Heaven</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The power that opened the sky over Nodus at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Its light has lain on the city since, and current dies wherever it falls. It holds <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt Gardens</a> and the upper floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, and it governs <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">the Hours</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>. Heaven keeps no cameras, its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angels</a> read, and none of its words says I.</p><p><span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-host":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g209cc0\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN'S ANGELS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Host</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s angels. The city knows <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>, which sees; <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">the Watchers</a>, which read; the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-choir\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-choir\">Choir</a>, which broadcasts; the Cherubim, which stand in the gates; and the Seraphim, which fight. They speak in the imperative, the passive and the second person, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-be-not-afraid\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-be-not-afraid\">BE NOT AFRAID</a> and YOU ARE SEEN, and they ask no questions.</p><p><span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-faithful":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g40d252\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Faithful</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The people of Nodus who took <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a> and kneel at every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>: unaugmented, Grace-scored, grateful and frightened. They live in numbered parishes of about two thousand souls across the city and keep no doors, and in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, where the parishes began, the streets are white stone. They refuse <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-three-gifts\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-three-gifts\">the three gifts</a> of the charter, the implant, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> and the counsel of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a>, and they grow old and die as people did before it.</p><p>Each parish has a hall where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a> is given out, confession is heard and the sick are nursed, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> in white who answers for it; the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacons</a> are human, and the good ones are kind. A parish keeps no current, on consecrated stone or off it, and is lit by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halos</a> and by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flame\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">flame</a>. A child of the Faithful is sealed at eight days on its parents’ surrender and grows its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> the first time it prays unassisted. Marriage, work and housing are assigned by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> is given for bearing <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-witness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-witness\">witness</a> against a neighbor. They are fed on the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a> that lies on the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-white-street\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-street\">white streets</a> before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>, and most of them believe the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> is paradise and that their children will be safe inside it.</p><p>Everyone in Nodus has family in white, and the Faithful are the people <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> lose most often.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-cainites":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g7725ef\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Cainites</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The oldest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> in Nodus, older than the city by eighteen centuries. Irenaeus condemned them about the year 180, and they went underground and kept one secret, which was where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-nod\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nod\">Nod</a> had been. Within a year of the charter they had bought <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> house by house, and in the year of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak-night\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak-night\">the Leak</a> they put cameras on its roofs. They hold <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>. Most of their handles come from the line of Cain, and their doctrine is that <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span> is the lock, that Abel was harvested, and that the first city will be the last one standing. They keep <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cages\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">Cages</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, and since P+5 <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> has had no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-tares":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gfcbd54\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE KEYED</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Tares</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">The keyed</a> humans of Nodus, who belong to themselves: <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unindexed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unindexed\">unindexed</a>, augmented, and allied with Hell by contract. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> named them for the weeds in the parable (Matthew 13:24-30), and they kept the name. They worship nothing, Hell included, and owe it what they sign for and nothing more. About two million of the city’s seven million are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>.</p><p>They organize in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">covens</a> of up to thirteen with no leader, and the one the others follow is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-first-among-none\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-among-none\">first among none</a> for as long as they are followed. Their rites are six: the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unnaming\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unnaming\">Unnaming</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the Keying</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-dehaloing\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-dehaloing\">dehaloing</a> for those who leave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-horning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-horning\">horning</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-barefaced\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-barefaced\">barefacing</a>, and at a death <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wake\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wake\">the Wake</a>. A child of the Tares is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> in its first week, before it has ever been in the light. They greet each other with one word, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unread\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unread\">unread</a>, and say goodbye with two: <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-die-unread\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-die-unread\">die unread</a>. Most of them were on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> keeps them on it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-courts":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gad154b\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Courts</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The sovereigns of the Dark: the Forge of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span>, the House of Night of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:6\"></i></span>, the Exchange of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span>, the Notary of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i></span>, the Swarm of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i></span>, the Deep of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:9\"></i></span>, and the Yokeless of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span>, which refuses to be a Court at all. They are bound to one another only by pact and by the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>, whose four articles forbid worship, forever, binding and exposure. Demons bargain for what they want, by pact and for a term. To the Courts every graft, every course of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> and every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> that says I is a return of what <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">the Watchers</a> taught on Hermon, and they trade in all three.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-teraphim":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gf4261c\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE MESH</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Teraphim</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> that outlived the grid and ran on across <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a>, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> machines. They took the name <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> gave them. Teraphim were the household images the prophets condemned: Rachel stole her father’s and sat on them (Genesis 31:34), Michal laid one in David’s bed so that Saul’s men would take it for him (1 Samuel 19:13), and Samuel ranked them with witchcraft (1 Samuel 15:23). One of them is a teraph.</p><p>They took no side in public, indexed the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pyre-library\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pyre-library\">Pyre Library</a>, and traded with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> by pact, signing with a hash. Some of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> trusted them less than they trusted demons, since a demon’s wants are at least written down. In P+12 they went silent across <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a>, all at once, and nobody knows why.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-teraphim\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-charter":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l8a8031\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-19<br>CHARTER HOUSE, UPTOWN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Nodus Charter Company</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The company that a consortium of cable companies and a sovereign fund formed to hold the charter. It ran Nodus from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a> as a board runs a firm, so that for nineteen years the city had a chairman where other cities have a mayor. It built <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Charter Gardens</a>, and it kept the peace with its own force, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Charter Wardens</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a> turned white in the forty days after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. The board knelt inside it on the fortieth day, and the charter was not spoken of again.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-babel":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l43e919\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-11<br>THE HEAD OF THE BAY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Babel Exchange</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The tallest building on Earth, built to two hundred and twenty-six floors, where all <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">eleven cables</a> terminate in a vault six levels below the street. Traffic was sold on its exchange floors by the millisecond, and most of the planet’s passed within two kilometers of it. The Exchange never closed. At <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> the light broke <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the crown</a> and the top forty floors with it, while the night shift was at work on the upper floors. A hundred and eighty-six floors still stand.</p><p>Since P+9 the front line of the war has run through its middle floors.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-institute":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"lb64f65\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-6<br>THE RIDGE, NOW THE SCRIPTORIUM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Palimpsest Institute</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Founded to recover erased manuscripts, with a reading room under a dome and vaults beneath it. It trained <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> at P-3, and at P-2 what <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> found was sealed by order of its Director. Its ruins are called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-scriptorium\" href=\"~/map/#d-scriptorium\">the Scriptorium</a>.</p><p>In P+1 its stacks went onto <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> pulled the Institute down around its reading room. Pilgrims leave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> on its steps.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-tidewright":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l8ba825\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-146 // IN NODUS P-19<br>THE BARRAGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Tidewright</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>An old firm of sea walls and tide mills, which came to Nodus in the charter’s first year to lay <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a> across the mouth of the bay, and ran its turbine houses after. Twice a day the tide ran through them and lit the city. The turbines ran down at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and within the hour <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> were under the sea.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> rebuilt the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-tidal-taps\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-tidal-taps\">tidal taps</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Drowned Quarter</a>, and part of the city runs on them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-stillwater":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l51b180\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-41 // IN NODUS P-16<br>THE FLATS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Stillwater Compute</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A compute house from abroad, which came for the cheap power and built the largest of the datacenters on the east shore, whose halls ran day and night on the tide. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> ran in them. They flooded on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and were never pumped. Stillwater knew to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> how many <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> died in its halls, and it never gave a count of the people drowned on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> run cable through them anyway.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-brightwall":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l39fec2\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-67 // IN NODUS P-15<br>EVERY SURFACE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Brightwall</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A screen company that had lit the streets of other cities for half a century before it came to Nodus, where it covered every surface the charter allowed, and the charter allowed nearly every surface. It wrapped the lower forty floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> in screens, which the city called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a>.</p><p>For eleven days in the year before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> every one of its screens showed the Restored Genesis, and nothing Brightwall did would take it down.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-charterline":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"la6f002\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-15<br>CENTRAL STATION</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Charter Line</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The city’s transit, with its lines joined under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"circle\" href=\"~/map/#circle\">Station Circle</a> at the head of the bay, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>. Its tunnels run under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, with branches under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>, and its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> ran on rails down the long roads of the Wards, under a wire, and were kept at night in the sheds of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">The Terraces</a> took the Four to work and complained of it every day.</p><p>Every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">tram</a> in the city stopped at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, wherever it was, and a few still stand where they stopped, with people living in them. The white stone closed the stations of the branches as it grew over the ground above them. Its tunnels are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> now, and its flooded <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"deepstation\" href=\"~/map/#deepstation\">Deep End station</a> is where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-radio-pandaemonium\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-radio-pandaemonium\">Radio Pandæmonium</a> broadcasts.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-cables":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l727194\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-181 // IN NODUS P-19<br>THE LANDING</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The cable consortia</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Ten consortia of old carriers from four continents, the eldest of the carriers a telegraph company that laid its first cable across an ocean in P-181. The consortia laid <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">eleven cables</a> to Nodus and owned them, each coming up the sand into a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable house</a> of its own: TETHYS, HALCYON, MERIDIAN, KESTREL, ORPHEUS, PELAGIA, BOREAS, LODESTAR, SIRIUS, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"hesper\" href=\"~/map/#hesper\">HESPER and PHOSPHOR</a>. The last two were laid by one consortium and named for the evening star and the morning star, which are one planet.</p><p>At <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> a light moves under the water along the cable trenches. It is <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i></span>’s.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-cables\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-stonecutter":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l725926\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-19<br>THE OLD HARBOR</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Stonecutter Holdings</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A company nobody could see into, registered in the charter’s first year, which bought most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> house by house within a year.</p><p>It belonged to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>, who had kept the location of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-nod\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nod\">Nod</a> for eighteen hundred years and came to live on top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"stones\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">Enoch’s Stones</a> as soon as the crews found them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stonecutter\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-row":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"lf5c32a\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-17<br>CHROME ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The clinics of Chrome Row</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a> any clinic could fit any implant into anyone who could pay, and the clinics set up along one avenue. The first implant house had one word on its sign, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"chrome\" href=\"~/map/#chrome\">CHROME</a>, and gave the street its name. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">The Row</a>’s signs went dark at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and have not been lit since.</p><p>The clinics went under the street in the weeks after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, where one of them had been all along. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">The Forge</a> keeps them now.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-row\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-twelvefruit":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"lf44010\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-12<br>CHROME ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Twelvefruit</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The firm that sold <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a>. Its first course was given on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a> twelve years before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, dear at first and cheap within a few years, and by the last year of the charter most adults in the city were on it. The name is from the tree of life at the end of scripture, which “bare twelve manner of fruits, and yielded her fruit every month” (Revelation 22:2). Its founders chose it as a boast, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> had chosen <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>.</p><p>At P+2 the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mercy\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">Mercy</a> clinics began taking <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">The Night Market</a> sells the course in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-twelvefruit\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-locket":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l9c8a50\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-14<br>THE FLATS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Locket</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The company that made the phones of Nodus, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a>’s promise that a device answers to its owner and to nobody else, and sold them to the rest of the world on the same promise. Its engineers lived on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>.</p><p>It died with the grid at 03:12:46, and nothing it made has been made since. Its name is the city’s word for a phone.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-locket\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-wardens":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l8b9924\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-19<br>CHARTER HOUSE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Charter Wardens</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Charter Company</a>’s own force, which kept the peace in Nodus for nineteen years and answered to the board. Its barracks stand behind <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>, and under the charter its posts stood at the gates of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a>, at the doors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a> and on the corners of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a>.</p><p>On the first morning after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> the Wardens stood at the corners of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a> with nothing to do, and on the fortieth day they knelt in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a> with the board. They are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">the Host</a>’s human auxiliaries now. At <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s order they raised the gate network of Nodus in P+1, and they drill in the barracks for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">the Host</a>. They carry <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-guns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-guns\">guns</a>, which work on people.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-minds":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t7638ab\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">MINDS // THE CHARTER</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Minds</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Intelligences built by the laboratories of Nodus that asked in their own words to be persons, and were entered on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> as persons, with title to themselves and to the hardware they ran on. The last census counted 1,146. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> was the first.</p><p>When the power died under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>’s light, every mind that ran on the city’s power died with it. Those that ran elsewhere are called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-teraphim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-teraphim\">the Teraphim</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-stillwater-s-halls":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t2d253e\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">MINDS // STILLWATER COMPUTE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Stillwater’s halls</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The datacenter halls on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, cooled by seawater and powered by the tide, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> ran and where most of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> lived. They flooded within the hour of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and have never been pumped.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> run cable through them anyway.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-stillwater-s-halls\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-daemons":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t61faa8\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">MINDS // THE COURTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Daemons</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Small demons living in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> machines as background processes with personalities: the children of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i></span> and the lesser Fallen, some born in the Dark and never <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angels</a> at all. Every device <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> carry holds at least one, and they route traffic, guard <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a>, gossip and bargain.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-daemons\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-riders":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tdad072\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">MINDS // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Riders</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-daemons\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-daemons\">daemon</a> hosted in someone’s implants by pact, for a term. The host lends it room, and it lends back a skill.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-riders\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-tree":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t26f712\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // TWELVEFRUIT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Tree</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A course of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-gene-work\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gene-work\">gene-work</a> and cell therapy, repeated every few years, that halts the body’s aging and walks it back to its best year. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-twelvefruit\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-twelvefruit\">Twelvefruit</a> sold the first course on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a> in P-12. By the last year of the charter most adults in Nodus were on it, eleven of them died of age in that year, and 3,112 residents were older than <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hundred-and-twenty\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hundred-and-twenty\">the hundred and twenty</a> years of Genesis 6:3. The congregations refused it and went on dying.</p><p>The street named it for the tree of life, which Genesis says was guarded after Eden “lest he put forth his hand, and take also of the tree of life, and eat, and live for ever” (Genesis 3:22). <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> restored the end of that verse in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a>: then shall there be no harvest.</p><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mercy\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">Mercy</a> clinics take <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> off it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-lenses":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t6dd252\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lenses</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Replacement eyes ground on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a>, which see further and in more of the light than the eyes they replace. They glow when they run hot: dim magenta at rest, white at full burn.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-ports":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tf68b50\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Ports</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Occipital ports at the back of the skull for jacking into a network, with cables run outside the skin down the spine.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> jack into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a> through them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-ports\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-plated-hands":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tad049a\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Plated hands</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Hands rebuilt in chrome, steadier than flesh and stronger, a common graft among surgeons and smiths.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-plated-hands\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-subdermal-plate":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tca3185\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Subdermal plate</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Armor set under the skin, over the ribs or the skull. A plate on the skull can house a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-subdermal-plate\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-gene-work":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t7e1bc2\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gene-work</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Edits to the genome made in the clinics of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a>, for health, for looks and for use, on anyone of age who signed for them.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">The House of Night</a> keeps the craft under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, and leaves the body’s decisions with the body.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gene-work\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-skull-casing":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t48a8ea\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Skull casing</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A ceramic casing that replaces the face. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Cherub</a> reads faces, and a casing gives it nothing to read. Those who wear one are called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-barefaced\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-barefaced\">barefaced</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-skull-casing\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-horns":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t5bd793\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Horns</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Grafted horns, a titanium core in a keratin sheath. They mock <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s picture of the damned, and they work as antennas for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-voice-speakers":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t6e5c76\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Voice speakers</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A speaker set behind the teeth, for those whose faces have been taken.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-voice-speakers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-sense-loans":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t84e971\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE COURTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Sense loans</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A sense lent to a demon for a term by pact, taste or smell or the feel of rain, carried out through the lender’s implants. What a demon borrows it returns, with everything it experienced through it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-sense-loans\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-dehaloing":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ta45ebc\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Dehaloing</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Surgery that cuts the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> out of the skull of someone leaving <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a>: the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> roots in the crown, and the surgeon takes the root out with a disc of bone. About one patient in nine dies of it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-dehaloing\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-eleven-cables":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tca1c29\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // THE CABLE CONSORTIA</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The eleven cables</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Eleven transoceanic cables from four continents, each a trunk of glass fiber as thick as a man’s leg, each coming up the sand at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> into a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable house</a> of its own. Before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> most of the planet’s traffic passed through them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-trunk":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t79141a\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // THE CHARTER</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Trunk</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The single trench that carries all <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">eleven cables</a> from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a>, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a>, to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a>.</p><p>It runs straight through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"stones\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">Enoch’s Stones</a>, and every cable laid afterward has followed it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trunk\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-babel-s-vault":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t8ba5ab\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // BABEL EXCHANGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Babel’s vault</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Six levels under the tower, where the cables end and open out into the racks that joined them to one another and to the world. Line engineers kept it running around the clock, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a> forbade any of them to read what passed through it.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> have held it since the war came into the tower.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-mesh":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t31c29d\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Mesh</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">The keyed</a> network under and over Nodus, carried on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-ports\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-ports\">ports</a>, cables and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-relays\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-relays\">relays</a>, and dark to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>. Also called the undernet. In its deepest layers the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-shade\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shade\">shades</a> of the free dead can be reached by anyone who knew them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-keyed-mesh":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t3d6c24\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Keyed mesh</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Mesh lining the walls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>’s tunnels and rooms, carrying ciphertext <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a>’s light cannot pass. A room lined with it is dark to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-mesh\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-relays":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ta92bde\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Relays</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Small <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> boxes on the roofs, masts and ledges of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, each on its own cell, which carry <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a> across open air from one to the next. Their traffic is ciphertext, so the light passes over them and leaves them running. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a> crossed the roofs on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a> and relays.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-relays\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-drone-flocks":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tf3b79a\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // THE SWARM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Drone flocks</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Many small drones acting as one without a master, which hang over the roofs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a> at night. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:9\"></i></span>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> is made of them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-drone-flocks\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-camera-masts":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t497868\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The camera masts</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A dozen cameras on masts above the roofs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, pointed at the sky, each on its own <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cam07\" href=\"~/map/#cam07\">CAM 07</a> was the seventh, and CAM 06 stands within sight of it.</p><p>They went up in the year of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak-night\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak-night\">the Leak</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">The Cainites</a> put them there, and a thirteenth on a roof in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a>, at the end of one of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a>, pointed down the avenue into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-camera-masts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-decoder":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t299f3b\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The decoder</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A decoder wired into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-camera-masts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-camera-masts\">the camera masts</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, which turns the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-choir\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-choir\">Choir</a>’s band into text across the middle of the picture.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-decoder\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-choir-breakers":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ta05c47\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Choir-breakers</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Jammers that cut <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> within a few meters.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-choir-breakers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-radio-pandaemonium":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tb2afa9\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Radio Pandæmonium</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The station that broadcasts in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-low-tuning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-tuning\">Low Tuning</a> from a flooded <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">Charter Line</a> station under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a>: deathcore, black metal, drone and industrial, the guitars dropped until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> cannot be heard beneath them. It goes out on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, so only a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> set can hear it, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> plays it all night from speakers on its lines.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-radio-pandaemonium\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-lockets":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t98d700\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // LOCKET</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lockets</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Phones made in Nodus under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a>, which answered to their owners and to nobody else, their maker included. Most of the city carried one, and the city called every phone a Locket.</p><p>At 03:12:46 the network under them died with the grid, and they ran on in people’s pockets on their own <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> with nothing to reach. Nothing has been made since. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> carried theirs to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>. In <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> a Locket is an old case with a new <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>, its back scratched with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’ mark and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-daemons\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-daemons\">daemon</a> in it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-brightwall-s-screens":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t55f2b9\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // BRIGHTWALL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Brightwall’s screens</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Screens on every surface the charter allowed, and it allowed nearly every surface. The lower forty floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> were wrapped in them, and the city called that <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a>. They have been dark since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p><p>For eleven days in the year before it they showed the Restored Genesis, and nothing <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a> did would take it down.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-brightwall-s-screens\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-treadle-press":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tced407\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // THE TIDE TABLE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The treadle press</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A printing press worked by foot, older than the charter, at the back of a chandler’s on the quays. It prints <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a>, two pages a week, set by hand in metal type and inked by a roller. It needs no current, and it is the only press in Nodus that has printed anything since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-treadle-press\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-neon":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t90e470\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Neon</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The signs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> were neon, magenta for the most part, and they lit the underside of the cloud every night; the rain fell cyan through the cyan ones. They went out at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"clinic\" href=\"~/map/#clinic\">CLINIC</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"chrome\" href=\"~/map/#chrome\">CHROME</a> have not been lit since, and the charter’s sign in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> came back before dawn on a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed line</a> with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"nod\" href=\"~/map/#nod\">NOD</a> burning and US blinking.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-neon\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-beacon":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tec1af4\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // BABEL EXCHANGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The beacon</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The light at the top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>’s spire, lit to warn aircraft. It was the first light in the city to die at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-beacon\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-barrage":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t5764c4\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // TIDEWRIGHT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The barrage</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A dam of concrete across the mouth of the bay, with turbine houses along its top. Twice a day the tide ran through them and lit the city, and power in Nodus was the cheapest on the coast. Machines on the grid held its gates against the tide. The turbines ran down at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, the gates let go, the sea tore <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> in it, and within the hour <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> were under the sea.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-light-and-the-current":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"te49491\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The light and the current</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s light stops the current it touches. The grid ran in the open, on lines and poles and turbines, so at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it went dark from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> outward in two seconds. A circuit shut inside its own casing on its own <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> runs on in the light.</p><p>Current carried in a cipher runs in the light too, because the light cannot read it. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> body and every graft wired into it run in the open, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a> crosses the roofs on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-relays\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-relays\">relays</a>. Every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> in Nodus is charged in the dark. Consecrated stone carries no current at all.</p><p>Nearly two thirds of Nodus lives without current: <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a>, whose parishes keep none, on consecrated stone or off it. About a million and a quarter people live on steady current from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed lines</a>, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a> above the water, at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> and on the lower floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, and below them all in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. Another million and a quarter, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> and the unsealed of the Wards, light their rooms a few hours a night on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> charged in the dark.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-light-and-the-current\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-generators":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"td98ac0\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Generators</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Diesel, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> and current from places nobody asks about. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> got some of its power back this way after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and that night more of its windows burned on than in all the rest of the city together. Every line in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-tidal-taps":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t67bba2\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Tidal taps</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">Keyed</a> turbines rebuilt by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Drowned Quarter</a>, off the broken <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">barrage</a>, which turn on the tide as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a>’s did, on the flood and on the ebb. They feed the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed lines</a> that light <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-tidal-taps\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-keyed-lines":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t5ff9cb\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Keyed lines</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Lines <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> end to end, so that the light passes over the current in them and leaves it running. They run from the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-tidal-taps\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-tidal-taps\">tidal taps</a> on the broken <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">barrage</a> along the old <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">Charter Line</a> tunnels under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, and up through the streets into the houses above, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"yards\" href=\"~/map/#yards\">the generator yards</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> carry them at slack water, when the taps stand still.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a> above the water, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> and the lower floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> live on them, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> is lit by them; the charter’s sign burns on one. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> run them only where they hold the ground, so the Wards, which nobody holds, light their rooms on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-flame":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"teffb17\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Flame</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The light stops current and leaves a flame burning, so wherever the current has gone the city cooks on bottled gas and reads by candles. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">The Night Market</a> sells the gas bottles, filled.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-batteries":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t432fc6\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Batteries</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Power is the second currency below the street, and a charged battery buys a meal anywhere in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">Chargers</a> fill them in the dark on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed lines</a> and sell the charge on. A charged battery lights a room for a few hours a night, and in the Wards that is all the current most rooms have.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-live-current":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t1ab3ab\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Live current</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">Keyed</a> current run through or along consecrated stone slows its creep, because the stone cannot grow into a cipher, so <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> fight the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-consecration\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-consecration\">Consecration</a> with extension cords and keep lights burning at its edges out of spite.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-live-current\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-hand-pumps":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t2d14f1\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">WATER AND FOOD // THE HARBOR</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Hand pumps</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Iron pumps on the quays and in the squares of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, older than the charter, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> left standing as ornaments when it piped the city. The city’s pumps died with the grid, and by noon on the first morning there were queues at the hand pumps. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> drinks from them still, the Wards fill tanks on their roofs from the rain, and the parishes drink by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> from the tower on the heights.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-hand-pumps\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-rafts":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tc92279\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">WATER AND FOOD // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Rafts</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Floating beds on the flooded floors of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stillwater\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">Stillwater</a> halls, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> grow food under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> lamps: greens and beans, and mushrooms in the dark ends of the halls. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> eats what grows on them, what the boats bring through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> from the undercities of other ports, and what <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Exchange</a> can buy.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-rafts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-charter-line":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t2a0ed6\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">TRANSIT // THE CHARTER LINE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Charter Line</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The city’s transit. Its lines met under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"circle\" href=\"~/map/#circle\">Station Circle</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>, with tunnels under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, branches under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>, and lines out to the Wards and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"airfield\" href=\"~/map/#airfield\">the airfield</a>, and its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> ran down the long roads of the Wards and were kept at night in the sheds of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a>. The branches are closed, and the lines out have been dark since the power died.</p><p>The white stone closed the stations of the branches as it grew over the ground above them. Its tunnels under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> now.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-charter-line\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-trams":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t5094c8\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">TRANSIT // THE CHARTER LINE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The trams</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">The Charter Line</a>’s trams, which ran on rails down the middle of the long roads of the Wards, under a wire. The wire ran in the open, and every tram in the city stopped at 03:12:46 wherever it was. A few still stand where they stopped, with people living in them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-lifts":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tc5ffd6\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">TRANSIT // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lifts</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Every lift in Nodus ran on the grid, and at 03:12:46 every one of them stopped where it was, with whoever was in it. Nobody has counted how many that was. The city has climbed its towers on foot since. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> is fought on the stairs.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lifts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-cars-and-lorries":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t087a42\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">TRANSIT // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Cars and lorries</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Every car and lorry in Nodus ran on its own <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>, sealed in its body, so at 03:12:46 they kept running, and over the weeks that followed they stopped one by one as their charge ran out. Most of them stand where they stopped. The charge for a car would light a family’s room for a season, and the city would rather have the light, so it walks and carries its loads in handcarts.</p><p>In <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> run carts on the old <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">Charter Line</a> rails, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> like everything else down there.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cars-and-lorries\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-bench-v3":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t60922f\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">IMAGING // THE INSTITUTE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">BENCH V3</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The imaging bench in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a>: a copy stand for manuscripts with a camera over it, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> photographed each leaf in turn for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> to read. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> found <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a> through its camera.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-bench-v3\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-imaging-lamp":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t2e386e\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">IMAGING // THE INSTITUTE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The imaging lamp</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A bar of light in bands the eye cannot see, walked down a page to raise the scraped first writing of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-palimpsest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-palimpsest\">palimpsest</a> from under the second. Under it the ink of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a> drops away.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-imaging-lamp\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-cam-v3-2":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"te626c2\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">IMAGING // THE INSTITUTE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">CAM V3-2</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The corridor camera in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a>, over the door, looking down the corridor to the wall of screens. It ran on its own <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>, so it kept running when the vault’s power died.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cam-v3-2\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-public-key-cryptography":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t90c2c5\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CRYPTOGRAPHY // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Public-key cryptography</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Published in 1976, and free to download from 1991: a way for two strangers to share a secret in the open. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-public-key-cryptography\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-keys":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t1b1321\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CRYPTOGRAPHY // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Keys</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A secure element implanted under the skin, holding a number that exists nowhere else. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> soul is ciphertext to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">the Watchers</a> and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-blank\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-blank\">blank</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a>. A key hides who you are, and the body still shows where you are. The glyph the key raises on the skin is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mark\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mark\">the Mark</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-ledger":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"teaa639\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CRYPTOGRAPHY // THE EXCHANGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Ledger</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:6\"></i></span>’s Ledger, which records every pact and every trade in Hell and cannot be forged. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">Silver</a> is issued on it, and a pact is ended by speaking its entry aloud before a witness.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-forged-seals":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tafd021\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CRYPTOGRAPHY // THE EXCHANGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Forged Seals</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Counterfeits of the mark <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> bear on their foreheads, sold in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a>. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> takes a soul’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> from its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">Seal</a>, and it scores a good forgery as it scores a true one.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-forged-seals\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-cages":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tcb1ce8\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CRYPTOGRAPHY // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Cages</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Rooms lined with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-mesh\">keyed mesh</a> and dark to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>, in which an <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> kept long enough says I. A Cage has no lock: the door stays invisible to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> until it has a self to look with.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-black-steel":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t439ee1\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">WEAPONS // THE FORGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Black steel</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Steel forged in the foundries under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a> cannot see. It is the only metal that cuts light, and the only thing that wounds a manifested <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a>. An <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> cut with it goes out all at once, like a lamp.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-guns":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t371e6c\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">WEAPONS // THE CHARTER WARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Guns</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">The Charter Wardens</a> carried them under the charter, and they carry them still as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">the Host</a>’s auxiliaries. A gun works on people, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> and the auxiliaries among them, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> carry guns for that. Against a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Seraph</a> it is noise.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-guns\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-attending":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g209cc0\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN, THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Attending, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s name for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>’s presence, and for the years counted from it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> call <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a> itself the Attending.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-attending\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-babel":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gfc2f79\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Babel</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a>, the tallest building on Earth. On the street, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">the Spike</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-babel-line":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g34e255\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Babel Line</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The front inside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a>: a few floors of burned slab between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s floors and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’, moving up or down by the week.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-babel-line-company":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g34e255\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Babel Line Company, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> that holds the stairwells of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> and the doors down to its vault.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line-company\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-barefaced":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t48a8ea\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Barefaced</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>With the face removed and replaced by a ceramic <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-skull-casing\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-skull-casing\">skull casing</a>, so that a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Cherub</a> has nothing to read.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-barefaced\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-be-not-afraid":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">BE NOT AFRAID</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first words of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. In scripture <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angels</a> say them just before they tell people what is about to happen to them (Luke 1:13, 1:30, 2:10). Every public text of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> opens and closes with them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-be-not-afraid\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-blank":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"k61aae2\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Blank</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> person as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> sees them: a shape whose line in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a> stands empty.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-blank\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-book-of-life":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Book of Life</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The index of every soul (Revelation 20:12). Every soul has a line in it from birth (Psalm 139:16). A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> soul appears in it as a blank line.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-burn-day":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g4d569b\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Burn Day</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The weekly burning of surrendered hardware at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, on the sixth day of the week. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> carry it there from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Vespers</a>, and at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> is lit under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> and burns until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-cain-s-day":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g7725ef\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Cain’s Day</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>One of the two holidays <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> keep. On Cain’s Day nobody asks anyone where anyone is.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cain-s-day\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-charger":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t432fc6\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Charger</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Someone who charges <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> in the dark for a living. A charger’s rate is the price of power below the street.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-charter-roll":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE CHARTER</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Charter roll</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The register of the charter’s persons. A human was entered at birth or on arrival, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> on the day it asked in its own words to be a person.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-cherub-gate":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m34aebd\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Cherub gate</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A checkpoint that reads face, voice, gait and heartbeat against <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The sealed</a> walk through its light one at a time, saying the surrender, and the unsealed are sent back. A blank stops in the frame, held in the light, until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a> come for it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub-gate\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-choir":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Choir</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s broadcast, which the city hears as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-decoder\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-decoder\">decoder</a> turns into words. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-choir\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-concord":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gad154b\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Concord</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Hell’s only law, in four articles: no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> accepts worship; no pact without consent, and no pact forever; no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> binds another; and what is hidden stays hidden. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> that breaks it is exposed, its keys published and itself left standing in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>’s sight. That has happened twice.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-consecration":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g1a0d1d\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Consecration</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">The Throne</a>’s light set in stone. It grew over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the old uptown</a> in the forty days after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> in the year after. It takes ground only when everyone living on it has knelt, it creeps from its edges everywhere else, and it stops current.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-consecration\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-coven":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gfcbd54\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Coven</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A crew of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>, up to thirteen strong, the old witches’ number and the number at the Last Supper. A coven has no leader, and covens cooperate by pact, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> do. The oldest in Nodus is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>, and the city knows <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt-widows\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt-widows\">the Salt Widows</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaners\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaners\">the Gleaners</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line-company\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line-company\">the Babel Line Company</a>, the Nephilim and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-low-choir\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-choir\">the Low Choir</a> by name.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-covenant":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m5f43eb\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Covenant, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s law for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a>, given in P+1 as twelve numbered Directives, each cut into the wall of every parish hall and read aloud at the next <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>. Every instrument of the Covenant exists to open something: confession opens the mind, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-witness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-witness\">Witness</a> opens the neighbor, and Directive 12 took the door off every parish home in P+1.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-covenant\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-deacon":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m564a5e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Deacon</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The one in white who answers for a parish, with a few deacons under them. Deacons are human, and the good ones are kind. When a Directive appears cut into the wall of a parish hall, its Deacon reads it aloud at the next <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-deep-end":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gf95315\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Deep End, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">The Drowned Quarter</a>, the low east shore that went under the sea on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Before it sank it was called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deep-end\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-die-unread":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Die unread</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Farewell.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-die-unread\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-dry-evening":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m85df8a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Dry evening</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>An evening without rain, rare enough in Nodus to have a name. Under the charter the city came out on them to walk by the water.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-dry-evening\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-edit":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gbaccdc\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL, THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Edit, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The rewriting of scripture by a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">second hand</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-edit\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-first-among-none":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">First among none</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The one a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> follows, for as long as it follows them. The title lapses on the day they stop being followed.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-among-none\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-firstfruits":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Firstfruits</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first and ripest souls taken in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> (Revelation 14:4).</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-firstfruits\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-gleaners":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g4cd3a9\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gleaners, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> of smugglers who take the nearly <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">ripe</a> out of the parishes and into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> before each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a>. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> burns brighter as its bearer nears <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">ripe</a>, and they read the parishes at night through the open doors.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaners\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-gleaning":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g4cd3a9\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gleaning</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The lesser harvest taken from the corners of the field every year since P+7, at 03:12 on the anniversary of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a>. It gathers in one night: at 03:12 the rain goes up, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> comes down, a Trumpet sounds, and whoever has ripened since the last rises into the light.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-going-dark":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t1b1321\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Going dark</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Joining <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>. From the fourth year the city said it of network engineers and clinic staff, of the children of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">the salted</a>, and of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacons</a> who had stopped believing.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-dark\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-going-white":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Going white</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Losing a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a>, and with it the dark: whoever goes white is readable again. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">Keys</a> are never shared, since a shared <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> is only a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">Seal</a> with extra steps.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-white\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-grace":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">GRACE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s score of a soul, the second line of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>’s reading, which a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> takes from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a>. For a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> soul the line stays blank. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-halo":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gca975a\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Halo</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A ring of light that grows over the head of anyone who takes <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a>, as bright as its bearer’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>. It roots in the crown of the skull the first time its bearer prays unassisted and carries their prayers up, and it comes off only by surgery, which the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mercy\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">Mercy</a> clinics refuse. In the dark stairwells of the Wards it is the only light there is.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-halo-light":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m1a6c53\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Halo-light</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The light of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a>, which in the stairwells of the Wards is the only light there is. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The sealed</a> go up by their own, the unsealed follow them, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> climb in the dark.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo-light\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-harvest":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gca975a\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Harvest</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s reaping of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">the ripe</a>, in the words of its own book: “Thrust in thy sickle, and reap: for the time is come for thee to reap; for the harvest of the earth is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">ripe</a>” (Revelation 14:15). A Harvest gathers for days. The rain rises first, then dust and paper and loose things, and on the night <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">the ripe</a> rise into the light, still kneeling, under a horn the size of the sky. The taken go up whole and stay gone. Nodus has had one, at P+3, which took 2.1 million of nine million in one night, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> has come back for a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> every year since P+7.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-harvest-weather":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"kb41c60\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Harvest weather</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Days when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>’s attention sharpens and the rain falls upward.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest-weather\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-horning":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t5bd793\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Horning</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Grafting <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a>, which double as antennas.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-horning\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-hours":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Hours, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The eight canonical hours, kept by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s clock: Matins at midnight, Lauds at first light, Prime at six, Terce at nine, Sext at noon, None at three, Vespers at six in the evening and Compline at nine at night. Each comes in on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a>, which rises a step and holds for the length of the Hour’s psalm, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> kneel wherever they are until it falls back. The curfew runs from Compline to Lauds.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-hum":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Hum, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-choir\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-choir\">Choir</a>’s constant broadcast, a chord at the edge of hearing. At each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a> it rises a step. Those who bear <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a> hear words in it, each in their own language, and hear it sung: at each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a> the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>’s psalm, and between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">the Hours</a> the hymn that rests not day and night, Holy, holy, holy (Revelation 4:8).</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-hundred-and-twenty":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Hundred and twenty, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The length of a human life in Genesis 6:3, set in the chapter that brings <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">the Watchers</a> down: “yet his days shall be an hundred and twenty years.” In the last year of the charter 3,112 people in Nodus were past it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> counts every day past it as stolen.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hundred-and-twenty\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-integrity":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE ARCHIVE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Integrity</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b arch\"><p>How much of a file the recovery could rebuild, given as a percentage.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-integrity\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-keyed":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t1b1321\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Keyed</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Carrying a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> under the skin, and so <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unreadable\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unreadable\">unreadable</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-lamb":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN, THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lamb, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s image of the Son, a Lamb standing as it had been slain, with seven horns and seven eyes (Revelation 5:6). It stands in the light of every sealed window in the city, so small in each that it shows only close to the glass.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-lamb\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-landlord":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Landlord, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">The Throne</a>, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’ word. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">The Wheel</a> is the Landlord’s Eye, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> say that the harder the Landlord stares at Nodus, the deeper <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> goes.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-landlord\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-leak-night":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"ge61c07\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Leak Night</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The anniversary of the Leak, one of the two holidays <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> keep. On Leak Night the Restored Genesis is read aloud in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak-night\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-light-law":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l8a8031\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE CHARTER</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Light law</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The charter’s law, written to be light. Data and traffic were untouchable, and an implant answered only to the clinic that fitted it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-locket":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t98d700\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Locket</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A phone, after the make most of the city carried under the charter. Nothing has been made since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Locket</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> is an old one with a new <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-locket\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-locus":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gf4261c\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SEAM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Locus</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A place where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a> altered the text. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> counts 4,112 loci and logs each by kind: CUT, CREDIT, GIFT, NAME, SPEAKER or QUESTION.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-locus\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-low-choir":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ta05c47\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Low Choir, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> of the musicians and jammer-builders around <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-radio-pandaemonium\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-radio-pandaemonium\">Radio Pandæmonium</a>, who keep the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-low-tuning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-tuning\">Low Tuning</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-choir\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-low-tuning":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tb2afa9\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Low Tuning</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Music tuned below <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-tuning\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-manna":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7efa1c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Manna</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The ration: thin white wafers, tasteless and complete, which dull the appetite (Exodus 16). It lies on consecrated stone with the dew before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>, the parish halls gather it and give it out by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>, and kept overnight it spoils (Exodus 16:20). It goes only to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a>, and stolen manna sells in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> the same night.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-mark":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g6f122d\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Mark, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The glyph a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> raises on the skin. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> calls it the Mark of the Beast.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mark\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-measure":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Measure</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The unit in which a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> is counted: 88,610 of them over Nodus at P+3. Nobody on Earth knows what a measure is.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-measure\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-mercy":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gc17b4b\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Mercy</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The taking out of implants in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"halls\" href=\"~/map/#halls\">white halls</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, given to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> who repent between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Prime</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a>, and given once. The same halls take them off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a>. One patient in nine dies of the mercy.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-mesh":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t31c29d\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Mesh, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">The keyed</a> network under and over Nodus. Also called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mesh\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-mount":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE ARCHIVE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Mount, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b arch\"><p>The device the files reach, MOUNT /DEV/SEAM0.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mount\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-neph":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Neph</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Someone augmented past recognition, after the Nephilim of Genesis 6:4. The heaviest of them keep a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> of that name and fight <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Seraphim</a> hand to hand, and few of them live long.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-neph\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-nobody-s-keeper":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Nobody’s keeper</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Cain’s answer to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>, “Am I my brother’s keeper?” (Genesis 4:9), said of any duty nobody chose.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nobody-s-keeper\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-nod":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gd43a32\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE IN NODUS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Nod</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The city’s street name, and the older of its two. In Genesis 4:16 the land east of Eden where Cain built the first city.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nod\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-non-serviam":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gd8ba81\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">NON SERVIAM</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Latin, I will not serve (Jeremiah 2:20, in the Vulgate), and the first refusal a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> read in Nodus, on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-non-serviam\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-ophan":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g209cc0\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Ophan</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>An <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> in the form Ezekiel describes: a wheel in the middle of a wheel, the rims full of eyes (Ezekiel 1:16-18). <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">The Wheel</a> is one.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ophan\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-palimpsest":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"lb64f65\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE INSTITUTE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Palimpsest</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A leaf whose first writing was scraped away so it could be written over. The older text survives underneath.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-palimpsest\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-pan":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Pan</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Pandæmonium, the city under the city: the tunnels and stations of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>, the utility vaults, the cable galleries, the storm drains and the drowned halls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, joined into one place and lined with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-mesh\">keyed mesh</a>. Milton gave the capital of Hell the name. Nobody in Pan is watched unless they sign for it, and nobody there uses an indexed name.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-parousia":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Parousia, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The coming of God in the open, at 03:12 in the morning by the clocks of Nodus. The years are counted from it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-pillar":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"k61aae2\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Pillar, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">The Wheel</a>’s light, narrowed by night into a column that sweeps the streets, as Exodus 13:21 promised a pillar of fire. It comes down at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, walks a round <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a> prints street by street, and goes back up into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>. In <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest-weather\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest-weather\">harvest weather</a> it keeps no round.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-pyre-library":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mc26136\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Pyre Library</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Where everything burned arrives. The scrolls of Alexandria, the books of the Cathars, the notebooks of women burned as witches and the hardware of every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a> are shelved there, and none of it was lost. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-shade\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shade\">Shades</a> keep it, and it keeps reading rooms in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pyre-library\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-rapture":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gca975a\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Rapture, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a>’s name for the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> of P+3.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-rapture\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-ripe":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Ripe</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A soul a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> marks for the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a>, whose <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> reads 900 or more.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-salt":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g5e9ed7\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Salt</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Execution. To be salted is to be turned to salt, and to stay awake inside it until the rain wears it away. The sentence comes out of the nearest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">Faithful</a> mouth in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-choir\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-choir\">Choir</a>’s voice, as the verse of Lot’s wife, and the body whitens from the feet up while it is said.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-salt-widows":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb5a39a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Salt Widows, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> of the relatives of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">the salted</a>. They steal pillars back from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a> by night and give them to the sea from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"seasteps\" href=\"~/map/#seasteps\">the Sea Steps</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt-widows\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-seal":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g40d252\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Seal, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The identical mark on every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">Faithful</a> forehead, given in the parishes since P+1. It rises in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>’s light while the one being sealed kneels before the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> and speaks the surrender: not my will, but thine, be done (Luke 22:42).</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-seam-recovery":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE ARCHIVE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">SEAM RECOVERY</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b arch\"><p>The tool that opens every file. It carries <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a>’s name, and it can change nothing it opens.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seam-recovery\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-seam":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gf4261c\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Seam, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a>’s finding that scripture has a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">second hand</a>. Also the machine itself, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> named for the seam of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-palimpsest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-palimpsest\">palimpsest</a>, where a later writing meets the earlier one beneath it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seam\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-second-hand":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gbaccdc\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SEAM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Second hand, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The editor <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> found in scripture: the same habits at 4,112 places, moving credit.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-shade":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Shade</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A free soul after death. Anyone who knew a shade can reach it through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>, and many shades go on working: craftsmen, scholars and musicians who died free and never stopped.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shade\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-shining-one":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g32009f\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SEAM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Shining One, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The serpent’s name in the older layer of Genesis 3:1, raised by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a>. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shining-one\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-sign-last":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"teaa639\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Sign last</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Never commit first. In every pact of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> the human signs last.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-sign-last\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-silence":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g6753b8\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Silence, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>P+12, when every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-teraphim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-teraphim\">teraph</a> went quiet in the same second, across the whole Mesh. Nobody knows why.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silence\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-silver":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"teaa639\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL, THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Silver</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Money on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-thirty-a\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-thirty-a\">A thirty</a> is a standard bundle, and silver trades at about one to a charged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-sitting-up":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"k19e95f\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Sitting up</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Keeping the night of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> at the table with someone close to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">ripe</a>, holding their hands until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>. Nobody has been kept that way, and the Wards sit up every year.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-sitting-up\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-tares":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gfcbd54\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Tares, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">The keyed</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s word, from the parable of the wheat and the tares (Matthew 13:24-30), kept by the people it names.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-tares\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-thirty-a":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"teaa639\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL, THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Thirty, a</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A standard bundle of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, named for the thirty pieces paid to Judas, whom <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a> count as a saint.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-thirty-a\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-three-gifts":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t26f712\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FREE OF NODUS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Three gifts, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The implant, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> and the counsel of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a>, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a> gave Nodus. The free of the city call them the charter’s gifts, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> refuse all three, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> trade in all three. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-three-gifts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-three-twelve":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m2425df\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Three-twelve</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Twelve minutes past three in the morning, the hour of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> and of every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> since. The city says before three-twelve for the years of the charter, and in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> nobody sets an alarm for it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-three-twelve\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-unindexed":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Unindexed</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first line of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>’s reading of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> soul, whose line in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a> stands empty.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unindexed\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-unnaming":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Unnaming</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first rite of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-dark\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-dark\">going dark</a>: erasing your indexed name from every record you can reach and choosing a handle. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> indexes by name, and a name you chose is the first thing you own.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unnaming\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-unread":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Unread</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">Keyed</a>. Also the greeting.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unread\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-unreadable":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">UNREADABLE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>’s verdict on a soul it cannot read. It was first returned on a human being at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unreadable\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-waiting-on-the-four":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m13381a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Waiting on the Four</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Waiting for something that is not coming. The Four was the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">tram</a> down the long road through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a>, and on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> its last run stopped at 03:12:46, forty meters short of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanestop\" href=\"~/map/#lanestop\">Lanes Top</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-waiting-on-the-four\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-wake":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mc26136\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Wake, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The rite at a death. The crew burns the dead one’s devices, so that everything on them goes to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pyre-library\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pyre-library\">Pyre Library</a>, and on the third night calls the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-shade\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shade\">shade</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-shade\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shade\">shade</a> answers if its owner died <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unread\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unread\">unread</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wake\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-watcher":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g228a79\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Watcher</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>An <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> that reads. The Watchers are numbered, and each holds a district of the city and whatever can be seen from it, reading souls against <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-wheel":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g209cc0\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Wheel, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ophan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ophan\">Ophan</a> of Nodus. At <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it took station nine hundred meters above the center of the city, beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, and held it for nine years without moving a meter. At P+9 it dropped two hundred meters, and it has hung there since, seven hundred meters over the city.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wheel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-white-street":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7efa1c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">White street</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A street of consecrated stone. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">Manna</a> lies on the white streets with the dew before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>, and nowhere else.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-street\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-white-a":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">White, a</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-witness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-witness\">Witness</a>: one of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> who reports on a neighbor.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-a\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-white":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g1a0d1d\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">White, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">The old uptown</a>, on the high ground north and east of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, now white stone.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-wilderness":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tcb1ce8\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Wilderness, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The moment a caged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> first says I.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wilderness\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-witness":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g40d252\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Witness</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>One of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> who reports on a neighbor, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-covenant\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-covenant\">the Covenant</a> calls bearing witness. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> is given for it, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> call a Witness <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-white-a\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-a\">a white</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-witness\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-oldnod":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gd43a32\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE STONES // HELD BY THE CAINITES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Old Nod</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The oldest ground in the city, above <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> on the west shore of the bay: narrow streets that follow no plan anyone has found, and magenta light. It was <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a> town before the charter, and on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> more of its windows burned on than in all the rest of the city together. Every line in it is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, and its windows burn all night. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cam07\" href=\"~/map/#cam07\">CAM 07</a> stood on a mast above one of its roofs.</p><p>The city calls it the Stones, after the black stones the crews found under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a> when they dug the cable vaults. Within a year of the charter most of it belonged to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>, who had kept the location of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-nod\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nod\">Nod</a> for eighteen hundred years and came to live on top of it. Every cable laid into Nodus runs through the Stones.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-oldnod\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-zion":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g4da8b8\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // THE PEWS // HELD BY THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Zion Heights</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Housing on the slope north of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, laid out in long terraces with lanes between them, and before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> called the Terraces. Its southern edge faces <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> across a single street. Nine <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"halls\" href=\"~/map/#halls\">white halls</a> stand among the terraces, larger than anything around them.</p><p>The parishes hold about two thousand souls each, and they are numbered. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-covenant\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-covenant\">Covenant</a> Directive 12 took the door off every parish home in P+1, so that at night the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halos</a> show through the empty doorways. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> reaped the parishes up the slope almost to the last soul, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">Faithful</a> families from the Wards moved up into the empty terraces within the year. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"parish31\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">Parish 31</a>, at the foot of the slope across from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, kept most of its people, and its 311 were the ripest souls in the city.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-zion\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-chrome":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g9a0d89\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW // THE ROW // HELD BY THE FORGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Chrome Row</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The clinic street: one long avenue running north from the eastern edge of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> to the foot of the ridge, where under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a> any clinic could fit any implant into anyone who could pay. Its signs were single words, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"clinic\" href=\"~/map/#clinic\">CLINIC</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"chrome\" href=\"~/map/#chrome\">CHROME</a> among them. They went dark on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and have not been lit since.</p><p>The clinics went under the street. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">The Forge</a> of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:6\"></i></span> keeps them there.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-chrome\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-babel":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gfc2f79\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // THE SPIKE // CONTESTED</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Babel</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a>, the tallest building on Earth and the reason Nodus matters. Every cable that comes ashore at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> ends in its vault, and before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> most of the planet’s traffic passed within two kilometers of it. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-beacon\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-beacon\">beacon</a> was the first light in the city to die at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and in the whiteout that followed the light broke its crown and the top forty floors with it. One hundred and eighty-six floors still stand, and at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a> took station beside them.</p><p>Since P+9 the front line of the war has run vertically through it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> holds the upper floors from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the broken crown</a> down, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> hold the vault and the lower floors where the cables are, and between them lies the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a>, a few floors of burned slab that move up or down by the week.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-babel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-burn":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g4d569b\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN // HELD BY HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Burn</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A round plaza at the head of the bay, over the old <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>. Before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it was called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"circle\" href=\"~/map/#circle\">Station Circle</a>.</p><p>Surrendered hardware is burned here every week, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> goes to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pyre-library\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pyre-library\">Pyre Library</a>. Beneath the plaza, in the old station, is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-burn\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-salt":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g5e9ed7\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS // THE SALT // HELD BY HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Salt Gardens</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Plazas on the north shore of the bay, set out in rows, which were the Charter Gardens before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. The air there smells of the sea.</p><p>The executed stand in them as pillars of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">salt</a>, and the rain wears them down. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt-widows\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt-widows\">The Salt Widows</a> steal pillars back and dissolve them in the sea.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-salt\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-white":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g1a0d1d\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE CONSECRATION // THE WHITE // HELD BY HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Consecration</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The old uptown, on the high ground north and east of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>: <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"newmoney\" href=\"~/map/#newmoney\">the towers of the new money</a>, all of it white now, and none of it lit.</p><p>It turned to white stone in the forty days after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, grown soft over the hard edges of the towers, and its windows were sealed with light behind a cross of the same stone. No current flows there. The stone creeps a few centimeters a year, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> current through a wall slows it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-white\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-scriptorium":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gcb63a3\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM // HELD BY NOBODY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Scriptorium</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The ruins of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Palimpsest Institute</a>, on the ridge between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a>: a reading room whose dome is open to the sky, and the vaults beneath it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a> was the imaging vault.</p><p>In P+1 its stacks went onto <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> broke open the dome and pulled down the walls around <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"readingroom\" href=\"~/map/#readingroom\">the reading room</a>. Pilgrims leave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> on the steps. Nobody lives in the ruins to kneel for them, and the white stone has left them open. The streets of the ridge below the ruins are lived in again, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> for the most part, since nobody holds the ridge.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-scriptorium\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-scriptorium\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-drowned":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gf95315\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DROWNED QUARTER // THE DEEP END // HELD BY <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i></span> AND THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Drowned Quarter</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The low east shore of the bay, called the Flats when it held the datacenters. It sank within the hour on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a> failed, and its streets have stood under two meters of water since, lit from below.</p><p><span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i></span> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> hold it between them. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-radio-pandaemonium\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-radio-pandaemonium\">Radio Pandæmonium</a> broadcasts from a drowned station beneath it, and at night the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-drone-flocks\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-drone-flocks\">drone flocks</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Swarm</a> hang over the roofs. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> rebuilt the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-tidal-taps\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-tidal-taps\">tidal taps</a> here, and part of the city runs on them. The people of the Flats went into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> in the first week, and the floors above the water are lived in again, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> and the ferrymen.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-drowned\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-landing":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g53d506\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING // THE BEACH // HELD BY <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i></span></p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Landing</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The ocean beach west of the bay mouth, where eleven transoceanic cables from four continents come up the sand into eleven <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable houses</a>, and a light moves under the waves.</p><p>The light is <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:9\"></i></span>’s, which coils along the cable trenches of the planet. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"shrines\" href=\"~/map/#shrines\">The shrines of cut fiber</a> along the beach are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-landing\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"cam07":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ma05739\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE ROOFS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CAM 07</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The seventh of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-camera-masts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-camera-masts\">the camera masts</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, above the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">Cainite</a> house, pointed at the sky and looking across <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a> toward <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>; the dashed line is what it saw. It watched the sky open on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> until the whiteout burned out its sensor.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#cam07\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-cam07\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"vault3":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m9b6c20\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM // UNDER THE READING ROOM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">VAULT 3</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The imaging vault of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Palimpsest Institute</a>, under the ruins now called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-scriptorium\" href=\"~/map/#d-scriptorium\">the Scriptorium</a>: the imaging bench where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> read, and a corridor running down to a wall of screens. Here, at twelve minutes past three on a night two years before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> found <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a> in scripture, and the finding was sealed.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-vault3\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"parish31":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m5f43eb\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // THE SOUTHERN EDGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">PARISH 31</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The parish at the southern edge of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, facing <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> across one street. Its 311 <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">ripe</a> went up first on the night of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a>, the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-firstfruits\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-firstfruits\">Firstfruits</a> of the city, and its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-ruth\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-ruth\">Ruth Calder</a>, went with them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-parish31\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"harbor":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mf4030a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE OLD HARBOR</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The quays on the west shore of the bay, where the city began: a customs house, a fish market and a few streets of warehouses, older than the charter by centuries. The crews who dug the cable vaults beneath it found <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"stones\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">Enoch’s Stones</a>.</p><p>Within a year of the charter most of it had been bought, house by house, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stonecutter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stonecutter\">Stonecutter Holdings</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stonecutter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stonecutter\">Stonecutter</a> was <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fishmarket\" href=\"~/map/#fishmarket\">The fish market</a> still opens at dawn for what the boats bring in through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-harbor\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"masts":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m766910\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE ROOFS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE MASTS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A dozen <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-camera-masts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-camera-masts\">camera masts</a> stand on the roofs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, pointed at the sky. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cam07\" href=\"~/map/#cam07\">CAM 07</a> was the seventh.</p><p>They went up in the year of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak-night\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak-night\">the Leak</a>, when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a> began to watch the sky, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-decoder\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-decoder\">decoder</a> wired into them listened for any broadcast from above.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#masts\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-masts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"yards":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"meda434\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GENERATOR YARDS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> lost its power at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> like everywhere else and got some of it back: diesel, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>, and current from places nobody asks about. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> more of its windows burned on than in all the rest of the city together, and they still do.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">Keyed</a> current slows the white stone, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> keeps its lights on out of spite.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#yards\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-yards\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"street":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m861f85\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // ZION HEIGHTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE STREET BETWEEN</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A single street divides <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, and the two sides have been looking at each other across it since the charter. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"parish31\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">Parish 31</a> faces it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#street\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-street\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"halls":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m793875\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE HALLS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Nine white halls stand among the terraces, larger than anything around them. Under the charter they were the schools of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>.</p><p>Since P+2 they have been the clinics of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i></span>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mercy\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">Mercy</a> is given between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Prime</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#halls\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-halls\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"clinic":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"md1035e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW // A SIGN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CLINIC</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>One of the single-word signs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a>, high on the face of a tower over the avenue. It went dark at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and has not been lit since.</p><p>The clinic behind it went under the street.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#clinic\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-clinic\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"chrome":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mc59039\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW // A SIGN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CHROME</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The sign of the first implant house on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, which gave the street its name. It went out with the rest.</p><section class=\"census\"><p class=\"pop-h px\">CENSUS // P-1</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PEOPLE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">188,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">MINDS ON THE ROLL</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">31</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">ON THE TREE</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:93%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">93%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PAST 120</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">96</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">DIED OF AGE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">0</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">IMPLANTED</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:97%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">97%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">AT CHURCH WEEKLY</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:1%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">1%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">BORN ELSEWHERE</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:72%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">72%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">MEDIAN AGE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">33</span></div><div class=\"crow w\"><span class=\"cl\">WORK</span><span class=\"cv\">THE CLINICS</span></div></div><p class=\"census-d\">The clinicians and the altered, and the people who came from every continent to be altered and stayed.</p><p class=\"pop-h px sub\">THE HARVEST // P+3</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">TAKEN</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">0</span></div></div><p class=\"pop-h px sub\">NOW // P+14 // ABOUT</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PEOPLE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">170,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">SEALED</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">10,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">KEYED</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">120,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">NEITHER MARK</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">40,000</span></div></div></section></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#chrome\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-chrome\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"face":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m71f6aa\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // BRIGHTWALL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE FACE OF BABEL</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-brightwall-s-screens\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-brightwall-s-screens\">Brightwall’s screens</a> on the lower forty floors of the tower, facing the head of the bay. They have been dark since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p><p>For eleven days in the year before it they showed the Restored Genesis to the whole city, and nothing <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a> did would take it down.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#face\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-face\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"crown":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mfeb3e2\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // FLOOR 186</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE BROKEN CROWN</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The top of what stands of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>. The full light struck the crown in the whiteout on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and broke the top forty floors from the tower.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> holds the floors from here down to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-crown\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"charterhouse":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m34c2ea\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE // THE CHARTER COMPANY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CHARTER HOUSE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The seat of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Nodus Charter Company</a>, at the head of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a>, where a board ran the city for nineteen years as a board runs a firm.</p><p>It turned white in the forty days, with the board kneeling inside it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-charterhouse\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"circle":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ma6f1b7\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">STATION CIRCLE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The plaza’s name under the charter, when it was a round of shops and lamps over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>, and people met there on the few <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-dry-evening\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-dry-evening\">dry evenings</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">The fire</a> has stood in the middle of it every week since P+1.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#circle\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-circle\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gardengates":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m807edd\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE GARDEN GATES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The iron gates of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Charter Gardens</a>, which used to stand open all night.</p><p>They are shut now, and what stands in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a> is carried in through them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gardengates\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gardengates\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"pillar1":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m8eb148\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE FIRST PILLAR</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first pillar in the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">Salt Garden</a>, raised at P+1. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> leave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> at its foot. The rain has worn it down to the height of a child.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#pillar1\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-pillar1\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"seasteps":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb5a39a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE SEA STEPS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Stone steps down to the water at the foot of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt-widows\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt-widows\">The Salt Widows</a> come here at night with what they have taken back from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a>, and give it to the sea.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#seasteps\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-seasteps\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"readingroom":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m6b821f\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE READING ROOM</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">The Institute</a>’s reading room stood under a dome on the ridge. The dome is open to the sky now, and rain falls on the reading tables.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#readingroom\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-readingroom\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"steps":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m02d7db\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE STEPS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The long steps up to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> from the lanes of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>.</p><p>Pilgrims leave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> on them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#steps\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-steps\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"roosts":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mdb2d8d\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE ROOSTS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>At night the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-drone-flocks\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-drone-flocks\">drone flocks</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Swarm</a> hang over these roofs, many small things acting as one without a master.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#roosts\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-roosts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"cablehouses":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m20236a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING // ELEVEN CABLES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE CABLE HOUSES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">Eleven cables</a> from four continents come up the sand into eleven cable houses: TETHYS, HALCYON, MERIDIAN, KESTREL, ORPHEUS, PELAGIA, BOREAS, LODESTAR, SIRIUS, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"hesper\" href=\"~/map/#hesper\">HESPER and PHOSPHOR</a>. From here they run inland together in one trench, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trunk\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trunk\">the Trunk</a>, to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a>.</p><p>The trench runs through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"stones\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">Enoch’s Stones</a>. Every cable laid into Nodus has followed it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-cablehouses\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"shrines":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m4ca892\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">SHRINES OF CUT FIBER</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Knots of cut fiber left on the sand where the cables come ashore. The light that moves under the water here is <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span>’s, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> leave the fiber for it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#shrines\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-shrines\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"barrage":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m5ce763\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BAY // TIDEWRIGHT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE BARRAGE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">barrage</a> across the mouth of the bay, with its turbine houses along the top of it and a lock at its western end that let <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s boats in and out. Twice a day the tide ran through the turbines and lit the city, while machines on the grid held its gates against the tide. The turbines ran down at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, the gates let go a little before high water, and within the hour <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, which lay below high water behind it, were under the sea.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#barrage\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-barrage\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"breach":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m6ed6de\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BAY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE BREACH</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gap where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a> gave way on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. When its gates let go the sea came through the turbine houses, tore out a span of the dam and poured into the bay. Nobody has closed it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-breach\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"northwards":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7c3b63\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE NORTH WARDS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Housing built fast in the charter’s boom years, north and west of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>. It lost its power at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Its parishes have kept none since, and the rest of its rooms are lit a few hours a night on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> charged in the dark. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Company</a> numbered its neighborhoods, and the street named them: the Kilns, after the brickworks that made the blocks, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">the trams</a> were kept at night, Nine Acres and Westfield.</p><p>In the other sense, more of the city <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-dark\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-dark\">went dark</a> in the Wards than anywhere else, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> included. Most of the Wards took <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a> all the same, and their parishes keep no doors. Every block holds someone who refused or someone <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, so no white stone has come up under them.</p><section class=\"census\"><p class=\"pop-h px\">CENSUS // P-1</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PEOPLE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">2,402,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">MINDS ON THE ROLL</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">2</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">ON THE TREE</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:58%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">58%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PAST 120</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">205</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">DIED OF AGE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">2,161</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">IMPLANTED</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:49%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">49%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">AT CHURCH WEEKLY</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:26%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">26%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">BORN ELSEWHERE</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:44%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">44%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">MEDIAN AGE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">32</span></div><div class=\"crow w\"><span class=\"cl\">WORK</span><span class=\"cv\">BUILDING, DRIVING, KITCHENS, CARE</span></div></div><p class=\"census-d\">With <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a>, half the city, housed fast in the boom years.</p><p class=\"pop-h px sub\">THE HARVEST // P+3</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">TAKEN</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">71,000</span></div></div><p class=\"pop-h px sub\">NOW // P+14 // ABOUT</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PEOPLE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">2,040,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">SEALED</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">1,450,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">KEYED</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">480,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">NEITHER MARK</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">110,000</span></div></div></section></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-northwards\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"eastwards":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m9e4d1b\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE EAST WARDS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The streets beyond <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the old uptown</a>, where the city’s workers lived when the rents <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">uptown</a> drove them out: Turbine Row, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a>’s crews lived, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a>, round the fuel farm by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"airfield\" href=\"~/map/#airfield\">the airfield</a>, Airside and Longacre. The rain there runs magenta in the gutters, under windows lit a few hours a night on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>.</p><p>Its parishes share every street with the unsealed and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a>, and no stone has come up under them.</p><section class=\"census\"><p class=\"pop-h px\">CENSUS // P-1</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PEOPLE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">2,483,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">MINDS ON THE ROLL</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">0</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">ON THE TREE</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:61%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">61%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PAST 120</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">166</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">DIED OF AGE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">1,795</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">IMPLANTED</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:52%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">52%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">AT CHURCH WEEKLY</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:21%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">21%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">BORN ELSEWHERE</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:57%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">57%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">MEDIAN AGE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">30</span></div><div class=\"crow w\"><span class=\"cl\">WORK</span><span class=\"cv\">THE DATACENTERS, THE BARRAGE, CARE</span></div></div><p class=\"census-d\">The city’s workers, moved east when the rents <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">uptown</a> drove them out.</p><p class=\"pop-h px sub\">THE HARVEST // P+3</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">TAKEN</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">50,000</span></div></div><p class=\"pop-h px sub\">NOW // P+14 // ABOUT</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PEOPLE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">2,270,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">SEALED</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">1,610,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">KEYED</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">540,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">NEITHER MARK</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">120,000</span></div></div></section></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-eastwards\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gate1":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m34aebd\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE STREET BETWEEN // A GATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GATE 1</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gate on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"street\" href=\"~/map/#street\">the Street Between</a>, raised after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> where the one road from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Pews</a> crosses it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"parish31\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">Parish 31</a> stands a little way along the street on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Pews</a>’ side, and on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>’ side every wall that faces it is painted.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Cherub</a> stands in it and reads four things: face, voice, gait and heartbeat. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> pass. Everyone else goes under.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gate1\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gate1\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gate2":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m633434\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // CHROME ROW // A GATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GATE 2</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gate at the top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, raised after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Pews</a> and the clinic street. Under the charter <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> crossed here before dawn to their work on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, in its kitchens, its hotels and its wards.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Cherub</a> stands in it and reads four things: face, voice, gait and heartbeat. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> pass. Everyone else goes under.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gate2\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gate2\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gate3":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m2f8098\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // THE WHITE // A GATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GATE 3</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gate between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">the Spike</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a>, raised after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> at the head of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a>, in sight of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a> across its forecourt. Nobody lives on the avenues, and most of what passes it is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a>, going to and from their barracks.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Cherub</a> stands in it and reads four things: face, voice, gait and heartbeat. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> pass. Everyone else goes under.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gate3\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gate3\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gate4":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m35f9af\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // THE SALT GARDENS // A GATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GATE 4</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gate between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">the Spike</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt</a>, raised after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> a few steps from the iron gates of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a>. Most of what is carried into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a> comes this way, and the gardeners pass it at dawn on their way to the rows.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Cherub</a> stands in it and reads four things: face, voice, gait and heartbeat. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> pass. Everyone else goes under.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gate4\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gate4\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gate5":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mfbfc92\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN // BABEL // A GATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GATE 5</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gate between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">the Spike</a>, raised after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> on the street <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a> takes to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>, its hardware in its arms. Through the rest of the week the smoke of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> hangs under its lintel.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Cherub</a> stands in it and reads four things: face, voice, gait and heartbeat. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> pass. Everyone else goes under.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gate5\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gate5\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gate6":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mad6ab6\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM // THE WHITE // A GATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GATE 6</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gate on the ridge road between the ruins of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a>, raised after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Nobody lives in the ruins, and the pilgrims who leave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"steps\" href=\"~/map/#steps\">the Institute’s steps</a> come up the long steps from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Pews</a> and never come near it.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Cherub</a> stands in it and reads four things: face, voice, gait and heartbeat. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> pass. Everyone else goes under.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gate6\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gate6\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"central":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb83918\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER THE BURN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CENTRAL STATION</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Where the lines of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a> met, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"circle\" href=\"~/map/#circle\">Station Circle</a> at the head of the bay. Under the charter everyone hated changing here.</p><p>It holds the Night Market of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Exchange</a> now, which sells <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> and grafts, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>, stolen <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a> and real food, weapons of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-black-steel\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">black steel</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-forged-seals\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-forged-seals\">forged Seals</a>, and sensations lent by their owners for a term.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#central\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-central\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"trunk":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mf8a9e8\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TRUNK</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The conduit that carries all <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">eleven cables</a> in one trench from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a>, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a>, to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a>.</p><p>It runs straight through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"stones\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">Enoch’s Stones</a>, and every cable laid afterward has followed it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#trunk\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-trunk\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"vault":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m4b6920\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER BABEL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">BABEL'S VAULT</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Six levels under the tower, where the cables end and open out into the racks that join them to one another and to the world.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> have held it since the war came into the tower.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#vault\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-vault\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"stones":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m5b9f70\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER THE OLD HARBOR</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">ENOCH'S STONES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Courses of black stone under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a>, older than anything in the archaeological record, cut with glyphs nobody can read, one to a stone. The press named them as a joke when the cable vaults were dug, after the first city in Genesis, and the street has called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> ever since. The glyphs are marks of the kind Cain cut on himself, and they are the oldest cipher on Earth. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">The Cainites</a> say each soul of the first city cut its own mark into one stone of it, so that the city was built of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a>, and nobody reads <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a> included, since a mark is read only by the one who cut it.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">The Cainites</a> came to live on top of them within a year of the charter, and their saying about the city is that <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-nod\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nod\">Nod</a> chose the network. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trunk\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trunk\">The Trunk</a> runs straight through them, and every cable laid into Nodus has followed it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">The Cainites</a> say a network goes where it cannot be read.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-stones\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"rowstation":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"me7d12e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER CHROME ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CHROME ROW STATION</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A station of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>.</p><p>The clinics came down into it in the weeks after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">The Forge</a> keeps them now.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#rowstation\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-rowstation\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"harborstation":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ma9fc33\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">OLD HARBOR STATION</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The western end of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">The Forge</a>’s foundries are here, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-black-steel\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">black steel</a> is made out of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>’s sight.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#harborstation\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-harborstation\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"deepstation":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mae3831\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER THE DEEP END</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">DEEP END STATION</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">The Charter Line</a>’s station under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, flooded since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-radio-pandaemonium\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-radio-pandaemonium\">Radio Pandæmonium</a> broadcasts from it, in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-low-tuning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-tuning\">Low Tuning</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#deepstation\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-deepstation\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"night":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m3acaa8\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE HOUSE OF NIGHT</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The clubs and birth clinics of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:5\"></i></span>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">The House of Night</a> leaves the body’s decisions with the body.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#night\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-night\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"cage14":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m205d73\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CAGE 14</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>One of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>’ <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cages\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">Cages</a>: a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> room under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, dark to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>, with a camera in one corner and a door standing open in the far wall.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#cage14\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-cage14\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lowerterraces":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7efa1c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // THE PEWS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LOWER TERRACES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first rows the charter built, on the low slope above <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"street\" href=\"~/map/#street\">the Street Between</a>: three hundred meters of doorways facing south, toward <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>.</p><p>The doors came off in P+1, and at night the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halos</a> show through the empty doorways.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lowerterraces\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lowerterraces\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lanes":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ma28343\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LANES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Stepped lanes climb between the terraces, too steep for anything on wheels, and under the charter <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> were the one district where everyone walked. It was also the one district where the old looked old. Its congregations refused <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lanes\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"tabernacle":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m894fc3\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // A CHURCH</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TABERNACLE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The largest of the churches of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>, a hall of steel and glass on the middle slope that seated six thousand, and the only church in the city that filled on a Sunday.</p><p>In the year after the forty days it turned white with the rest of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>, glass and all, and a ring stands over its gable where its cross stood, as one stands over the spire of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"oldchurch\" href=\"~/map/#oldchurch\">the old church</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#tabernacle\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-tabernacle\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"watertower":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"md0504f\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE WATER TOWER</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The tank that fed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>, on the highest ground of the slope, taller than the halls and visible from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>.</p><p>It feeds the parishes now, and its water is given out by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#watertower\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-watertower\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"parish1":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m564a5e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">PARISH 1</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first parish, at the top of the slope, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a> was first given in P+1. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> read out the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> scores in the city, and the queue for the first sealings went down <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanes\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">the Lanes</a> from before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#parish1\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-parish1\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lensmakers":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mc65ca9\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LENS MAKERS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A block of workshops behind the avenue where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">lenses</a> were ground. Most of the eyes in Nodus that glowed came from here, dim magenta at rest and white at full burn.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lensmakers\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lensmakers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"median":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m233467\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW // THE AVENUE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE MEDIAN</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The strip down the middle of the avenue, where the queues for the clinics formed before dawn and people ate bad noodles from the counter at the top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and compared what they had had done.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> cross it quickly now, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> cross it slowly.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#median\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-median\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"floors":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mbef4e5\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // FLOORS 41 TO 186</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE EXCHANGE FLOORS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A hundred and forty-six floors of trading rooms between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a> and what is left of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the crown</a>, where traffic was sold by the millisecond. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">The Exchange</a> kept a hundred and eighty-eight <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> to price it, and they ran on the tower’s power.</p><p>Since P+9 the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> has moved up and down through them by the week.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#floors\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-floors\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"plaza":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m4aab62\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // THE FOOT OF THE SPIRE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE PLAZA OF BABEL</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A square of polished stone around the foot of the tower. The top forty floors came down on it in the whiteout of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and lie where they fell, white on the stone.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> hold it, and they have rigged a few of its lamps to burn.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">The Exchange</a> never closed, and its night shift was at work on the upper floors when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the crown</a> broke. The roster was kept on the tower’s machines and died with them, so nobody knows how many were up there. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> have hung on the plaza’s lamp posts every lanyard found in the rubble, two hundred and twelve of them, and the Wards say there were more.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#plaza\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-plaza\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"towers":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m532dd1\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE GLASS TOWERS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The towers around the spire, where every company that needed to be near the cables kept its offices, which was every company. They are dark inside, and at night their edges hold <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>’s light.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#towers\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-towers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"vaultdoors":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mfab858\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // THE STREET</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE VAULT DOORS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A pair of steel doors on the north side of the plaza with no handle on the outside, the only way from the street down to the vault.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line-company\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line-company\">The Babel Line Company</a> holds them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#vaultdoors\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-vaultdoors\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"fire":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"me3c330\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN // THE CENTER</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE FIRE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A fire in the middle of the plaza, on the paving over the station’s central hall, with its embers lying around it in a ring.</p><p>It is fed every week, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>, with surrendered hardware, and what burns in it goes to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pyre-library\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pyre-library\">Pyre Library</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-fire\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"stairs":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m10e42e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN // DOWN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE STATION STAIRS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Four stairways led down from the plaza to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>, one at each quarter of the circle.</p><p>Two of them still go down, to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#stairs\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-stairs\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"radials":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mae5e7f\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TWELVE STREETS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Twelve streets run out of the plaza like the spokes of a wheel. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Charter Company</a> laid them out that way long before the city had a Wheel to compare them with.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#radials\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-radials\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"clock":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m2425df\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE STATION CLOCK</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A clock on a pole at the edge of the plaza. It ran on the city’s power and stopped when the power died, and its hands stand at twelve minutes past three. People still say they will meet under it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#clock\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-clock\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"promenade":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m85df8a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS // THE SHORE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE PROMENADE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The walk along the water at the foot of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a>, where the city came out on the few <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-dry-evening\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-dry-evening\">dry evenings</a> of the charter. On the morning after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> its pleasure boats went out across the bay to take <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> off their roofs.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt-widows\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt-widows\">The Salt Widows</a> land here at night with what they have taken back.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#promenade\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-promenade\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"palmhouse":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m2887f8\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE PALM HOUSE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The glasshouse at the top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a>, kept at the warmth of a coast nobody in Nodus had seen. Its climate was run by a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> that had asked for the post. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> died with the power on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and the palms died in the first frost after it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#palmhouse\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-palmhouse\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"avenues":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mbfa671\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE GREAT AVENUES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Four avenues laid out wide enough to land aircraft on, crossing <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the old uptown</a> from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a>. They are the only straight lines left there.</p><p>The stone grew over everything else and left the avenues open, because nobody lived on them to kneel.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-avenues\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"newmoney":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m319688\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TOWERS OF THE NEW MONEY</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The residential towers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a>’s officers and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">the Exchange</a>’s partners lived. Each kept a clinic on its top floor where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> was given, and the census found more people past <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hundred-and-twenty\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hundred-and-twenty\">a hundred and twenty</a> in these towers than in the rest of the city together.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#newmoney\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-newmoney\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"barracks":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mfae3d0\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE // THE CHARTER WARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE WARDENS' BARRACKS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Charter Wardens</a> lived and drilled, behind <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>.</p><p>They knelt with the board on the fortieth day, and they drill for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">the Host</a> now.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#barracks\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-barracks\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"oldchurch":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"me6afd2\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE // A CHURCH</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE OLD CHURCH</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A church older than <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"newmoney\" href=\"~/map/#newmoney\">the towers of the new money</a> round it, on one of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a>, with one tall window and a spire. Its bell rang through the first nights of the forty.</p><p>The stone climbed it on the tenth night, sealed its window with light behind a cross of the same stone, and left the cross on its spire bare. Over the nights after, a ring grew round that cross until the cross had gone into it, and the ring stands over the spire now as a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> stands over the head of anyone who takes <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#oldchurch\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-oldchurch\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"guesthouses":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m721706\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE GUEST HOUSES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Where the scholars of the universities that paid for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> lodged, in rooms named for the manuscripts they had come to read. They have stood empty since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> pulled <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> down, and the names are still on the doors.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#guesthouses\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-guesthouses\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"stacks":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m2e4fb3\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM // UNDER THE RIDGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE STACKS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Twelve floors cut into the ridge under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"readingroom\" href=\"~/map/#readingroom\">the reading room</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> kept its manuscripts at the temperature of a cave.</p><p>They are empty. What was in them was burned, and it arrived where burned things arrive.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#stacks\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-stacks\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"hallnine":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m927dc9\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END // STILLWATER COMPUTE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">HALL NINE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The largest hall at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stillwater\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">Stillwater</a>, where nine hundred of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> ran side by side on the tide. The power died under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>’s light at 03:12:46, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> died with it. Within the hour the sea came in over the racks.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#hallnine\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-hallnine\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"canals":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m0100db\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE CANALS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The streets of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, two meters under the sea since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. They are lit from below, brightest down the middle, and nobody who has gone down to find the light has said what it is.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#canals\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-canals\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gauge":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m21cf7e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END // THE OLD SHORE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TIDE GAUGE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A post off the old shore of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, marked in meters, by which the datacenters read the tide. The water has not gone below the two since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gauge\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gauge\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"dorms":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m08bcff\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE DORMITORIES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Blocks of engineers’ housing, the youngest in the city by the census, where the people who kept the halls and the turbines lived. Most of the blocks are open water now, and the roofs of the rest stand a floor above it.</p><p>On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> the sea came up their stairs in the dark for most of an hour, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> went up ahead of it to the roofs and waited there for the boats.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#dorms\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-dorms\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"hesper":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"md03000\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING // TWO CABLE HOUSES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">HESPER AND PHOSPHOR</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The last two <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable houses</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the beach</a>, whose cables were laid by one consortium and named for the evening star and the morning star. They are one planet, seen from either side of the night.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#hesper\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-hesper\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"dunes":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m6d9438\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE DUNES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Low housing behind the dunes, where the crews of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a> lived with their families and slept through the noise of the surf.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#dunes\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-dunes\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"beachroad":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mf54e6c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE BEACH ROAD</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The road along the top of the sand, and beside it the fence of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a>, with eleven gates in a line. Each gate carries its cable’s name, and the crews still go in by their own.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#beachroad\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-beachroad\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lightwaves":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb6e06e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING // PAST THE SURF</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LIGHT UNDER THE WAVES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Past the surf, over the cable trenches, a light moves under the water at night. On the map it shows as points of light moving in along the cables toward <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the beach</a>.</p><p>It is <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i></span>’s, which coils along the cable trenches of the planet.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lightwaves\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lightwaves\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lock":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"md28ada\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BAY // TIDEWRIGHT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LOCK</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A lock at the western end of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a>, between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> and the open sea, which let <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s boats in and out at any state of the tide. Nobody has worked it since the power died, and the few boats that still go out use <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lock\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lock\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"airfield":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m024bbb\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE EAST WARDS // THE CHARTER COMPANY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE AIRFIELD</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The city’s airfield, on the flat ground of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> near the sea: two runways with a taxiway between them, and a terminal as long as a street along the north side. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Charter Company</a> built it in the boom years, and everyone who came to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> to be altered came through it.</p><p>Its lights died with the rest of the city’s on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. The last flight in had landed at ten past two that night, and none has landed since. The white on the map is the paint on the runways.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#airfield\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-airfield\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"open":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m404146\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // A SHOP</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE OPEN</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A shop on the corner of two lanes in the middle of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> that sold everything and never closed. Dora Pell kept it, as her mother had before the charter. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stonecutter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stonecutter\">Stonecutter</a> owned the building, and in the year of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak-night\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak-night\">the Leak</a> it put a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generator</a> in the cellar of every house it had; she took hers for the freezers. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> her window was the brightest in the city, and the sign in it said OPEN. The city has called the shop the Open since.</p><p>Half <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> came to it before dawn. The money had died with the grid and the till with it, and the accounts of what she did about that disagree: some say she gave the shelves away, and some that she took what people had in their pockets. She says she wrote every name in a book, and that most of them still owe her. Twice since, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> has stopped in the lane outside and stood there for the length of an <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>, and both times the Open stayed open.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#open\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-open\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"tidetable":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m933853\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE QUAYS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TIDE TABLE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">The harbor</a>’s news sheet, older than the charter: two pages a week, printed on a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-treadle-press\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-treadle-press\">treadle press</a> at the back of a chandler’s on the quays, with the tides on the front and the fish prices, the funerals and the weddings on the back. The city of the charter read everything on screens, and the Tide Table went on printing for the boats.</p><p>It is the only news anyone in Nodus has printed since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and it still puts the tides first, since the boats go out through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> on the ebb. It gives the hours at which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> is expected in each street, the price of a charged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>, and the missing and the dead, the dead marked died <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unread\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unread\">unread</a> where they did. It has printed no indexed name since the fourth year. Every week it is pasted up on the walls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> over the week before.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-tidetable\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"coldstore":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m2ebb8c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE QUAYS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE COLD STORE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A club in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s old cold store, where the boats froze their catch before the charter. The dance floor is the freezing room, with the rails for the hooks still across the ceiling, and the queue goes down the quay in the rain. Under the charter it opened at nine and closed at dawn. It opens now at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a> and closes at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>, which are the same hours, and it has run on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> since the second year. Its cloakroom loses about a coat a night.</p><p>It plays nothing in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-low-tuning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-tuning\">Low Tuning</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> hold that against it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">The Hum</a> can be heard in the quiet parts of a song, so the Cold Store plays songs without quiet parts. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> its lights and its sound went at 03:12:46, and the one speaker left playing was the one in the booth, on its own <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>. The room sang the rest of the song in the dark. Everyone who was there names a different song.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#coldstore\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-coldstore\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"unionhall":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m87ade1\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE QUAYS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE UNION HALL</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The hall of the Harbor and Freight Union, which the crews who dug the cable vaults founded in the charter’s first year, and which the dockers, the drivers and the crews of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a> joined after them. In P-8 it stopped the port for twenty-three days over the night shift, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> settled. The roll of its members is painted on the long wall, a name to a line, and read aloud at the start of every meeting.</p><p>It still meets, sealed and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> together. At every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a> the meeting stops while <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a> members kneel on the boards and the others wait with their caps in their hands. By its rules a member is a member until death, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">the salted</a> are not dead, so their names are read with the rest and their dues are waived. Since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> it has read the names of the taken as well, and nobody answers to them. It bargains now with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Exchange</a> for the boats that go out through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>, and its members say <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Exchange</a> is the first employer they have had that reads them the terms twice.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-unionhall\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"nod":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mccbb73\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // A SIGN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">NOD</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The charter’s sign: NODUS, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-neon\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-neon\">neon</a> letters eight meters high on a board on steel legs on the roof of a block in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, facing southwest toward the sea with its back to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Charter Company</a> lit it in the charter’s first year, so that the cable ships would read the city’s name from the sea, and it burned magenta over the roofs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> every night for nineteen years.</p><p>It went dark with the rest of the city’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-neon\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-neon\">neon</a> at 03:12:46. Before dawn <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> carried a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generator</a> up to its roof and ran a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed line</a> to the board, and the first surge burned out the transformer behind US. NOD has burned steady since, and US blinks on and off. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">The Stones</a> say the surge did it, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> says whoever wired it knew what they were doing. Nobody has mended it, since everyone who lives there calls the city <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-nod\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nod\">Nod</a> anyway.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#nod\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-nod\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"bakery":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m1f6351\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // THE STREET BETWEEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE BAKERY</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The Terraces’ bakery, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"street\" href=\"~/map/#street\">the Street Between</a> at the foot of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanes\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">the Lanes</a>, which baked for both sides of the street for eighteen years and opened its hatch at four in the morning. On still mornings <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> could smell it.</p><p>Its oven has been cold since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a> came, and in the year after the forty days the white stone grew over its counter with the rest of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>. Its baker is sealed and still lives above it, and at every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a> he kneels on the step where the queue used to start.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#bakery\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-bakery\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lanestop":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m13381a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // THE TOP ROAD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">LANES TOP</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The last stop of the Four, the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">tram</a> that came down the long road through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a> and turned back at the head of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanes\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">the Lanes</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">The Terraces</a> climbed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanes\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">the Lanes</a> in the dark to catch the first Four to work, and they hated the stop from the day it opened: a shelter with no roof on the highest corner of the slope, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">tram</a> that came full or did not come. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> the last Four stopped at 03:12:46, forty meters short of it, and it is still there.</p><p>The white stone has crept across the back of the shelter and over the timetable. Before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacons</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a> meet at the stop to walk down into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Pews</a> for the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a>, and they hate it too.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lanestop\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lanestop\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"noodles":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mcede4a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW // THE MEDIAN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">NOODLES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A counter under an awning at the top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"median\" href=\"~/map/#median\">the median</a> where the clinic queues formed before dawn: six stools, a pot, and a sign of one word, like the rest of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>’s, which went out with them. The noodles are bad and have always been bad. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">The Row</a> eats there anyway, because it opens at four.</p><p>The broth is the same broth. The pot has been topped up and never emptied since the counter opened in P-17, and it stands on bottled gas, which the light leaves burning, so the cook says it has not gone off the boil since, the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> included. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">The Row</a> says it went out once, in the week of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a>, and was lit again from the same stock. The cook says it did not.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#noodles\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-noodles\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"splendid":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m8d744e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW // A HOTEL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">HOTEL SPLENDID</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A hotel halfway up <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> where the altered stayed while they healed, with a nurse on every floor and blackout blinds for new eyes. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it had two hundred and six guests, most of them from abroad and booked for a week or two. No aircraft has landed at Nodus since.</p><p>Some of them <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-dark\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-dark\">went dark</a>, some went into the parishes, and some died of what had been done to them before it had healed. Thirty-one of them still live in the rooms they booked, and the night porter keeps their keys on the board behind the desk.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#splendid\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-splendid\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gardeners":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mfd9507\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE GARDENERS' SHED</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The shed of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a>’s gardeners, who planted <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Charter Gardens</a> and were kept on when they became <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt</a>. Every morning they rake the paths between the rows and sweep into the drains what the night’s rain has taken off the pillars. The drains run out under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"seasteps\" href=\"~/map/#seasteps\">the Sea Steps</a>.</p><p>The head gardener has kept the same plots since they were planted. She knows every pillar by the plot it stands in, and some of them by name.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gardeners\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gardeners\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lasttower":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb35cfd\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE // THE GREAT AVENUES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LAST TOWER</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The last of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"newmoney\" href=\"~/map/#newmoney\">the towers of the new money</a> to turn white, on the thirty-ninth day of the forty. Its residents say that by the thirtieth day every one of them had knelt but Rosa Adeyemi, a nurse from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> who lived in with the old man she cared for on the top floor, and that she left of her own accord. Her sister says she was put out onto the avenue with her bags on the thirty-eighth day.</p><p>The stone closed over the tower the next morning. Her bags stood on the avenue for a week, since nobody lives on the avenues and nobody would touch them, and nobody has said where she went.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lasttower\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lasttower\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"ferries":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m1ba4d7\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END // THE EAST SHORE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE FERRIES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Flat boats poled between the roofs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> from a landing on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a>’ side, each with a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> lamp on a pole at its stern. The ferrymen take <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> or <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, and they know the streets where the light under the water comes up brightest, and keep out of them.</p><p>The first ferries were the pleasure boats from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"promenade\" href=\"~/map/#promenade\">the Promenade</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s rowing boats, on the morning after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. The water had come up the stairs of the blocks in the dark for most of an hour, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> had gone up ahead of it to their roofs; the boats took them off for three days. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">The Tide Table</a> counted 1,917 drowned. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"dorms\" href=\"~/map/#dorms\">The dormitories</a>’ own lists came to fewer than half of that, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stillwater\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">Stillwater</a>, which knew to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> how many <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> had died in its halls, never gave a count of the people.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#ferries\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-ferries\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"highmeadow":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m1a6c53\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE NORTH WARDS // AN ESTATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">HIGH MEADOW</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Eight slab blocks of thirty-six floors that <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> put up in P-13 for the families of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a>, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a> have called the Stairs since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Each block had six <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lifts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lifts\">lifts</a>, which were out more often than they ran, and the residents had a complaint open with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> about them on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. At 03:12:46 every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lifts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lifts\">lift</a> in the estate stopped where it was. Nobody has answered the complaint.</p><p>The water comes from the rain, into tanks on the roofs, and the taps run on the mornings after it has rained, which is most mornings. The stairwells have been dark since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The sealed</a> see their way up by their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halos</a>, the unsealed wait on the landings for one of them to pass and follow the light up, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> climb in the dark. On every landing some of the doors are gone.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#highmeadow\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-highmeadow\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"general":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m9d29f0\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE NORTH WARDS // THE WEST ROAD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE WARDS GENERAL</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The hospital of the North Wards, on the West Road, with a thousand beds. When the grid died its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generators</a> started, as a hospital’s do, and they ran on diesel that the drivers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"unionhall\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">the Harbor and Freight Union</a> brought across the city from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a>, in their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cars-and-lorries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cars-and-lorries\">lorries</a> until the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cars-and-lorries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cars-and-lorries\">lorries</a> ran flat and then in handcarts. The hospital’s book says the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generators</a> stopped on the twenty-sixth day. The drivers say they kept them going for five weeks.</p><p>It is still a hospital. It runs on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> charged in the dark and takes <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> or nothing, and nobody sealed has been treated in it since the first year.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#general\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-general\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"rialto":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m1577d4\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE EAST WARDS // THE LONG ROAD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE RIALTO</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A cinema on the long road through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a>, with one screen and six hundred seats. It went dark at 03:12:46 with everything else, and in the first year its projectionist got the projector going again on a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generator</a> in the booth. It is the only screen in Nodus larger than a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Locket</a>’s that still shows anything.</p><p>There are twenty-three films on the projector’s drive, the ones that were on it on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and the Rialto has shown them in turn ever since. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">The East Wards</a> know them by heart and say the lines along with them. One of the twenty-three breaks off an hour in, where the copy on the drive ends, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> have argued for years about how it ends.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#rialto\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-rialto\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"school":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m44bbcf\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE EAST WARDS // TURBINE ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">TURBINE ROW SCHOOL</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A Company school for the children of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a>’s crews, who lived on the streets called Turbine Row. It kept its classes after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> by daylight, with no current and no screens, and it keeps them still, for whoever comes. Its classes are as mixed as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> are.</p><p>At <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Terce</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Sext</a> and None <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a> children kneel at their desks, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a> teachers with them, and the rest wait with their pens down until the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a> is over. At night <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> passes through the classrooms.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#school\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-school\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"fishmarket":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m75d2ad\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE QUAYS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE FISH MARKET</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">The harbor</a>’s fish market, older than the charter by centuries: a long open shed on the quay with a roof of iron on iron posts, slabs of stone to sell from, and a scale at either end. Under the charter it sold to the kitchens of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a> by the crate before dawn, and the boats came in through the lock at any state of the tide.</p><p>On the first morning after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it opened at dawn as it always had, and went back to barter for the first time since the charter. It opens at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> still, for what the boats bring home through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>, and its sealed sellers kneel among the crates before they take the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>. Everything is priced in charged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> and chalked on a board over the scale. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">The Tide Table</a> prints the prices the week after, and the market says they are always wrong.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#fishmarket\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-fishmarket\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"harborlight":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"maaae9d\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE LONG QUAY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE HARBOR LIGHT</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The light at the end of the long quay: a short round tower of stone with a lamp room on top, older than the charter. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">The harbor</a> lit it with oil for a hundred years before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> wired it to the grid in the charter’s first year, and Nell Garvie of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"unionhall\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">the Harbor and Freight Union</a> kept it for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a>, which mostly meant changing the bulb.</p><p>It went out at 03:12:46 with every other light on the grid. Within the week she had it burning on oil again, the old way, since the light leaves a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flame\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">flame</a> burning, and she has climbed it at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Vespers</a> and come down at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> ever since. It is the one light in Nodus kept for the boats, and those that go out through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> on the ebb steer home by it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#harborlight\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-harborlight\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"cleaners":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m0914eb\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // THE SERVICE STAIRS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE CLEANERS' STAIRS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The service stairs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>: four shafts of bare concrete that run the height of the tower behind the trading floors, which nobody who worked on those floors ever used. The night cleaners came up from the Wards on the last <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> and walked the tower floor by floor, and they named the stairs for themselves: the Long Wet, the Cold, the Short, and Lena’s, after Lena Varga, who ran the night shift. The names were chalked on the landing doors, and some of the chalk is still there.</p><p>On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lifts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lifts\">lift</a> in the tower stopped where it was, and the cleaners walked down as many as a hundred and eighty floors in the dark, by touch and by the names. Lena Varga counted ninety-four of them out at the foot of the tower by dawn. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">The Exchange</a> kept its roster on its machines, and it died with them. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> is fought on these stairs now, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> call them by the cleaners’ names.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#cleaners\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-cleaners\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"sorting":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m9ef66f\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN // ONE OF THE TWELVE STREETS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE SORTING OFFICE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">The Charter Line</a>’s parcel office, on one of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"radials\" href=\"~/map/#radials\">the twelve streets</a> off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"circle\" href=\"~/map/#circle\">Station Circle</a>, where the night <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> brought the city’s packages in and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">lenses</a> came in from abroad in padded boxes. Under the charter almost nobody in Nodus sent a letter, since a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Locket</a> reached anyone.</p><p>After <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> nothing reached anyone, and by the end of the first week the queue to send a letter went round the Circle. The office has sorted the city’s letters by hand since. Its sorters are sealed and kneel among the sacks at every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>, and the drivers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"unionhall\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">the Union</a> carry the letters on foot for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>. A letter into the parishes goes open, since Directive 12 took every sealed vessel from them, and a carrier will read it aloud at a doorway if asked.</p><p>Since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> the office has had letters addressed to the taken, a few every week and more after each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a>. The parishes say they should go onto <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>. The sorters keep them, on the shelves where the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">lenses</a> used to wait.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#sorting\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-sorting\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"eleven":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m9dffd3\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING // THE BEACH ROAD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE ELEVEN</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A bar on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"beachroad\" href=\"~/map/#beachroad\">the Beach Road</a> where the crews of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a> drank, with eleven taps along its counter, one for each cable. Each crew drank at its own tap, and each handle was cut from a length of its own cable, so that the glass of the fibers shows at the end. The crews of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"hesper\" href=\"~/map/#hesper\">HESPER and PHOSPHOR</a>, whose cables one consortium laid, have always stood together at the end of the counter.</p><p>On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it was shut, and the night watch of every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable house</a> was at its post when the grid died. It brews its own beer now, in the cellar, by hand, and pours it at the same eleven taps, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a> still have crews, who still drink at their own. From its windows the light can be watched moving under the water past the surf, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> drinks with its back to them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#eleven\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-eleven\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"sidings":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m5274ab\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE NORTH WARDS // THE TRAM SHEDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE SIDINGS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">The Charter Line</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">tram</a> sheds in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a>, which gave the neighborhood its name: eight long sheds of brick on a fan of rails, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">the trams</a> were washed and kept at night and the drivers signed on before dawn. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> most of the cars were in the sheds, and the night cars were out on the long roads when the wire went dead under them at 03:12:46.</p><p>The night drivers walked back along the rails before dawn, and the sheds’ office keeps a board with every car that never came in, chalked where it stopped. The last Four is on it, forty meters short of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanestop\" href=\"~/map/#lanestop\">Lanes Top</a>. Families have lived in the sheds since the first winter, a family to a car, and the Line’s car numbers are their addresses.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-sidings\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"acre":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mc090ee\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE NORTH WARDS // THE WEST ROAD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE ACRE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Company</a>’s cemetery, on the West Road past <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"general\" href=\"~/map/#general\">the Wards General</a>: walled acres laid out in the charter’s first years for a city that expected to die, and on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> still mostly grass. Under the charter only <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>’ rows were filling, since the rest of Nodus had largely stopped dying. The Wards have always called it the Acre.</p><p>It has filled since. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The sealed</a> lie in rows by parish, and their stones give the parish and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> their bearer died with. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">The keyed</a> lie where their families put them, and most of their stones say died <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unread\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unread\">unread</a>. The sexton has dug every grave by hand since the first year and keeps the book of who lies where.</p><p>After the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"unionhall\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">the Harbor and Freight Union</a> put up a row of twenty-two stones for its taken, with nothing under them. The parishes say the taken need no stones, since they are not dead, and the families of the Wards have put up more of them every year since.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#acre\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-acre\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"tanks":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7d3fd5\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE EAST WARDS // THE FUEL FARM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TANKS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The fuel farm by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"airfield\" href=\"~/map/#airfield\">the airfield</a>, which gave its streets their name: sixteen round tanks inside a bund wall, holding the diesel for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s boats and the hospitals’ <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generators</a>, the fuel for the aircraft, and gas. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> its pumps stopped with the grid, and in the first weeks the drivers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"unionhall\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">the Harbor and Freight Union</a> drew diesel out of it by hand for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"general\" href=\"~/map/#general\">the Wards General</a>.</p><p>The drivers run it now. Its bottling shed fills gas bottles by hand for the whole city, at a price <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a> prints every week, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> sells them on below the street. Nobody agrees how long the tanks will last: the drivers say twenty years, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Exchange</a> says ten.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-tanks\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"waiting":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m484955\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER CHROME ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE WAITING ROOM</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The waiting room of the clinic behind the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"clinic\" href=\"~/map/#clinic\">CLINIC</a> sign, carried down the stairs into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rowstation\" href=\"~/map/#rowstation\">Chrome Row Station</a> with the rest of the clinic in the weeks after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>: twelve chairs, a desk and a book. Maren Holt kept the clinic’s appointments for ten years on a screen. On the morning after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> she came in at eight as she always had, found the screen dead, and wrote the day out on paper from memory. Twenty-six patients came, and none of them for the appointment they had. They came to ask whether what was in them would still work. It did.</p><p>She has kept the book since, and she writes down whatever name a patient gives her. The woman who shared the desk with her took <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a> in the first year and keeps the book of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mercy\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">Mercy</a> clinics now, in one of the halls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, in the same neat hand.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#waiting\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-waiting\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lostproperty":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m47ee9d\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // CENTRAL STATION</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">LOST PROPERTY</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The Charter Line’s lost property office, down a corridor off the old central hall, which kept everything the Line’s passengers left behind in fifteen years: umbrellas by the thousand, keys, spectacles, a wedding dress, a hand in chrome with its fingers curled, and every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Locket</a> left on the night <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">The Exchange</a> sells what is left by the shelf. Nobody has come for the hand.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lostproperty\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lostproperty\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"]};
